 <wpt lat="43.656670" lon="-79.384580">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-02-27 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Canada Auto Parks</name>
  <desc>Moderator Note: Please confirm that it is OK to stay overnight in your vehicle.&#xA;.....&#xA;Parking lot in Toronto Downtown - it is a 20-30 minutes walk to the CN-Tower or just 2 blocks away from the next underground-station. Not the most beautiful place on earth but in the center and surprisingly quiet during the night - the workers on the nearby construction site waited until 9AM (!) to start with concrete drilling and other noisy things. We didn&#39;t ask if it is ok to stay in the car for the night and just did it. No facilities. We paid 65 CAN for 2 nights. Close to the CN-tower there are other parking lots as well so there are perhaps other options to stay downtown.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-02-27 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/8171 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
