  <ele>137.94905849178664</ele>
  <time>2022-08-16 14:12:13 UTC</time>
  <name>Kleanza Creek campground.</name>
  <desc>Turnoff to the W near km post 165. Approx. 6 km STEEP and narrow track down to the Tatshenshine river. One spot right at the shore but large gravel pad just behind. In season salmon fishing and bear/eagle watching.&#xA;&#xA;Approx. 1 km further (across bridge) on 4x4 track (if wet) to another even better spot with several campsites. This is also a put-in point for canoe/ raft trips to Glacier Bay (11 days)&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-16 14:12:13 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/20362 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
