 <wpt lat="50.450340" lon="-111.910640">
  <ele>767.7371826171875</ele>
  <time>2022-11-14 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kinbrook Island Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>A nice clean well-landscaped park. Not many places on iOverlander east of Calgary. $45Cdn a night with power which we do not need but the power sites are far superior to the others. We got one of the last 2 sites on a Friday. Seems like a local place with lots of giant rigs, boats and bikes. The lake has a nice beach. September 2022: C$ 35 shower 1C$ for 2 min.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-11-14 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/24911 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
