 <wpt lat="55.757320" lon="-97.833970">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-23 13:39:59 UTC</time>
  <name>McCreedy RV &amp; Tent Campground</name>
  <desc>Nice place.  Run by homeowners who live there.  Showers, electricity, dump and a nice grassy area for tents.  They have a phone#(206) 677-4837 and e-mail address but, in my experience in July 2016, the phone ain&#39;t gonna be answered.  Just go up there and it will be fine.  It is a nice grassy, laid-back campground.  Go up to the house and knock on the door to get someone to show you around.  Probably over 50 sites but only about 10 were occupied.  As I said, friendly. If you can&#39;t find anyone, just pull in, hook up, pitch the tent and eventually someone will be around. vehicle parking. $10 per day $50 per week Including pic- up and drop-off at train station. Don&#39;t leave your vehicle in Thompson unless you want to put in an insurance claim.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-23 13:39:59 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Unknown&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/35627 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.352190" lon="-97.352050">
  <ele>209.0</ele>
  <time>2022-09-01 11:49:43 UTC</time>
  <name>Scratching River Campground</name>
  <desc>Was here in July 2016.  This appears to be a city run park/rv park in sleepy, quiet, Morris, MB, Canada.&#xA; Really nice campground and taken care of.  But, when i was there, it was deserted.  Electricity was on, grass mowed, no trash, everything well kept and painted.  Just no people or rv&#39;s.  There was a payment box without envelopes, nice electrical rv hookups (where I charged my phone), small covered dining area and, the port-a-john was tipped over :(  I had to poop in the trees next to the campground :(  next to the river.  I guess you have to go into town and ask around who to talk to about rules and regulations and whatnot, and find out who will tip up the port-a-john for you.  I didn&#39;t do that, I&#39;m a guy but, I&#39;d stay again.    Congratulations to the groundskeeper, whoever it was.  Good job.  You need to get that port-a-john upright guys, pleeeeeeease.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-01 11:49:43 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/35628 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
