  <time>2023-08-09 17:22:19 UTC</time>
  <name>Beaver Lake Recreational Area</name>
  <desc>Very secluded campsite 6 miles off the highway on BC77.  Shaded sites and very primitive.  No cell signals and no services. Free camping. &#xA;---&#xA;There are few sites with picnic tables and fire pits. About 30 km North from Fort Nelson. Turn right on the junction to Liard highway 77, than continue about 10 km, it&#39;s on the right. Nice quiet place in the forest. And it&#39;s free, we asked at the visitor center. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-09 17:22:19 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/37343 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
