  <time>2024-06-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Incredible views 32mi after Haines Jct</name>
  <desc>Big deep puddle near the road. Too deep even for 4x4. There&#39;s a narrow gravel road heading south to sulphur creek. Leads to an open, flat area with a fire pit and the most amazing mountain views you can wish for. Plus a great wild life observation spot towards the creek. High chance of spotting moose or bears!&#xA;Better than places by Kluane Lake as this is hidden and further from the Alaska highway.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/38020 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
