  <ele>1371.54736328125</ele>
  <time>2024-07-15 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kiska/Willson public Land use Zone</name>
  <desc>Paved road loop with a gravel place in the middle on highway 11. Close to Banff and Jasper National Parks. Only few meters from the street but quiet. There is space for a few vehicles, stone fire rings. No toilets. Free! A Black Bear with two cubs was right in front of the driveway when we came to this place &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-15 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/38346 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
