  <ele>673.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Cutbank Tiver bridge</name>
  <desc>User-maintained Campground, that requires a AB Public Lands Camping pass since June 1, 2021. https://www.alberta.ca/public-lands-camping-pass.aspx&#xA;&#xA;We entered from the Northbound side rest area. Maximum 14 day stay. Some fire pits, a porta potty and garbage and recycling. Be careful if the grounds are muddy.&#xA;&#xA;There is currently a little food truck at the rest area&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/38601 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
