 <wpt lat="63.604818" lon="-135.901340">
  <ele>488.88720703125</ele>
  <time>2024-07-22 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>McIntyre Park Campground</name>
  <desc>Free campground situated directly at the river, just before you cross the bridge, few hundred meters before Mayo.  Five sites, at least two of them are pull-through sites, all have fire rings and picnic tables. Big shelter. Pit toilets. We&#39;ve been here in July and were the only ones. And even our cellphones had reception. There is another free campground right in town (Gordon Park, GPS ca.: 63.59555, -135.90090). &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-22 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/39989 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
