 <wpt lat="44.608513" lon="-79.360568">
  <ele>189.0</ele>
  <time>2023-05-05 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Hammock Harbor RV Park</name>
  <desc>Mostly permanent or semi-permanent seasonal trailers.  The grounds are well kept, especially the gardens that individuals have built up.  It is relatively expensive, and the showers and bathrooms are old and shabby.  You would think that for $264 per week they would provide hot water in the showers, but for only a quarter you can have some hot water.  The park is full of small canals and most people have a boat tied up next to their trailer.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-05-05 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/40854 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
