  <name>Waterton River</name>
  <desc>Nice spots just on the lower side of the Waterton Reservoir dam, across from the spillway. Two sites with fire rings separated by a mound of gravel. The area is used by locals for fishing - some visitors during the day.  (There is a provincial recreation area on the other side of the dam with a (paid) campground). &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-03-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/43070 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
