  <ele>224.0</ele>
  <time>2022-10-05 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Off Nass road by the Cranberry River </name>
  <desc>Nice dead end road that comes to a washed out bridge on the river.  Overgrown so no river views unless you don&#39;t mind an incline or you are in a tent. A few spurs on this road some short with a fire ring and others longer that we didn&#39;t explore.  super quiet and remote.  We drove 10k of Nass road without seeing a car.   Another 1k off that road to this spot &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-10-05 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/43340 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
