 <wpt lat="46.140252" lon="-60.197704">
  <ele>7.9</ele>
  <time>2024-06-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Sydney, gravel lot by the water </name>
  <desc>Large level gravel lot right by the water (boardwalk). Close to downtown.&#xA;&#xA;- 5min walk to Cruise Centre (toilets, fast wifi)&#xA;- 10min walk to YMCA, library,&#xA;- 15min to Sobey&#39;s (supermarket).&#xA;&#xA;There are public toilets on site, but apparently only open in summer (high season).&#xA;&#xA;Lot gets full and busy during business hours and quiet and dead empty at night. &#xA;Some locals sitting in their cars, drinking and listening to music in the evening, but no big party. If you want to stay away from them, park on the city side of the lot, away from the water.&#xA;&#xA;Stayed for five days and nights and didn&#39;t get bothered. Free.&#xA;&#xA;Disclaimer: Things might look different in summer (high season).&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/58571 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
