 <wpt lat="53.282060" lon="-117.778471">
  <ele>1164.607753753662</ele>
  <time>2024-05-29 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kinky Lake Campground </name>
  <desc>This is the first small lake within the Wildhorse Provincial Park. If you keep down the same road, you will get to the Wildhorse Lake Rec. site. The road in was quite rough, especially in the spring. The rec. site costs 23$ from May 1st until October 1st, but during the off season it’s free. Some of the sites are for reservations only, others are first-come first serve. &#xA;There is a beautiful view of the mountains, and the lake is stunning, blooming with marsh birds. They have a shed of already cut wood to use and fishing is allowed on the lake if you have the proper permit. Highly recommend for a good Alberta Rec. Site.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-29 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/58678 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
