  <time>2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Taylor Landing Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Good for one night and for free. Close to the Alaska Highway and next to the river. The view is not the best because on the other side of the river you see industry. No facilities. Enough space for at least two campers/RV‘s. Some people are coming around from time to time but we didn’t have troubles staying there (before the gate).&#xA;&#xA;User reports Nice view, but a lot of rusted nails on the ground.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/61356 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
