 <wpt lat="49.666140" lon="-117.285677">
  <ele>1156.6068121381104</ele>
  <time>2023-06-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Six Mile Lake Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Travel north from Nelson on highway #3A for 8.0 km to Six Mile Lakes road. Follow Six Miles Lakes road for 10.0 km to a fork in the road. Then take the right fork for 3.0 km to the recreation site . The road is suitable for a 2wd vehicles, although the last 3.0 km are very rough in sections. there are 4 tents pads and 4 picnics tables. Also good for camper vans, but I will not recommend to come with a trailer or RV as it is a single vehicule road, hard to turn around if needed. Really rough and slow to get here, but rewarding with the beautiful wilderness of the place. A lot of fish and beavers. No wifi. Free!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/62074 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
