 <wpt lat="45.116051" lon="-74.518133">
  <ele>23.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Cooper Marsh Conservation Area</name>
  <desc>Parking lot is just near a big beautiful garden with trees, picnic tables, and a pond. No facilities except pit toilets. Quite a lot of mosquitoes at night time. Nobody bothered us and it&#39;s free. Road is nearby but it&#39;s quiet at night. There are various walking trails around in the reserve, where you can observe the fauna. Drinking water used to be available but at the time we were there, the taps were broken. Dogs are allowed at the parking area but not inside the park.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/63620 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
