 <wpt lat="52.629630" lon="-117.864275">
  <ele>1207.9068507887423</ele>
  <time>2024-07-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kerkeslin Primitive Campground </name>
  <desc>We checked a few campgrounds close to Jasper on a Thursday, Whistler was closed, Wapiti and Wabasso were both fully booked , this is the only place with a few spots available, even on Fri evening, it is first-come first-serve , $24,75 including fire permit and firewood, with drinking water, pit toilet, cooking shelter, large site for our motor home, lots trees and very private , next to the river ! 25 KM from Jasper , a bit far but only 5 km to the Athabaska Water Fall! We loved it here! &#xA;Oh, and we just spotted a black bear strolling on the Campground. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/64120 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
