 <wpt lat="51.233124" lon="-115.506342">
  <ele>1473.4704490387812</ele>
  <time>2024-07-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Two Jack Main Campground </name>
  <desc>One of the few first come, first serve campgrounds around Banff Town. Surrounded by trees, the campground is not primitive, but simple (cooking shelter, food locker, dish washing station, kiosk, firewood, fire rings and picnic tables). Even though the washrooms have no showers, there is warm water and plug-ins. It&#39;s a 10 minute drive to town. In total 380 sites. 21,50$.&#xA;&#xA;Note: This is not the Two Jack Lake Campground which is 1km before this one and has reservation only! Since there is only limited parking in Banff Town, public busses go from the campground to town. I can recommend the nearby Johnson Lake for swimming! &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/64346 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
