 <wpt lat="49.486590" lon="-115.092640">
  <ele>1026.37451171875</ele>
  <time>2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Mount Fernie Provincial Park Campground</name>
  <desc>A user has reported: there is currently a boil water advisory for the campground.  Not listed on campground website.&#xA;&#xA;Great campground in a pine forest. Spotless Toilets and showers. Big overflow. If you want to stay there you should book in advance on a long weekend and in the holiday period. The price was something like C$ 30 per night.&#xA;&#xA;From the Campground you can start your trail. Here starts also your training for the XXL Mountain Marathon with 120km through the mountains. It&#39;s true just google it!&#xA;You should not be a railway hater. Trains hook their melodic horns night and day.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/64740 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
