  <name>Haynes Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Small campground on a peninsula in the lake Osoyoos&#xA;In the summertime you have to be an early bird to get one of the sites. &#xA;Exciting view. Good on hot summer-days because of a steady wind.&#xA;C$ 32 pn.&#xA;no tents in the overflow.&#xA;Car access closed in the winter.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-20 13:38:48 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/64742 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
