 <wpt lat="45.632259" lon="-64.855245">
  <ele>14.195386746940214</ele>
  <time>2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Dennis Beach </name>
  <desc>At the edge of the bluff that is eroding from traffic. Perfect view makes this a very popular site day and night that is subject to the patrolling of local man. Possible to walk down to the beach by trail near the entrance or drive down/fall over the slope and get stuck/hurt. Grassy area to camp/park on but riveted with back-hoe holes or piled up with slash to deter you. There was a fire-pit on the right away from trees (back-hoe operator pilfers soil here). Easy access for all rigs. Directly reachable from the 915. Only metres from the main road. No signs of traffic. at all. We stayed for an extra night. When it&#39;s windy, the trees and bush will give you decent wind protection. Watch out for used cat litter. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/64993 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
