 <wpt lat="48.648141" lon="-124.221942">
  <ele>202.052734375</ele>
  <time>2023-07-06 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>By the River (2)</name>
  <desc>Not far from the first spot are two more. Partly hidden from the road, next to a small, shallow river. Each spot with a fire ring and one even with a table/benches. Quiet but unfortunately some trash and mosquitoes around. A big rig might have problems to turn around, so back in if you are larger than a micro bus. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-06 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/65275 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.204040" lon="-124.032631">
  <ele>94.27433776855469</ele>
  <time>2024-03-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Jinglepot RV &amp; Campground</name>
  <desc>Well-maintained and nice campground in a lovely park like setting. Every site is visually separated by scrubs and trees, provides table &amp; benches as well as a fire pit. Lovely and sunny central floral garden w/chairs and mini fountain. Tent sites #19/18/17 etc. are close to shower (1$ for 4 min)/toilet block and receive good WiFi coverage. Most of these tent sites can be used by small RVs and camper vans too, but if using provided water or electricity, you get charged as an RV. We do have a rooftop tent and used the electricity, hence we’re charged $35 per night (lower prices available during low season). Not cheap, but fairly ok for what you get. Nice and helpful Korean owner, only downside is the noisy highway not far away. On the property there is a large indoor room with tables and books you can use for free, as well  as a kitchen sink for washing dishes. Moreover there is an on-site coin laundry (washing and dryer: equally $2 per load). Everything very clean. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-03-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/65277 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="51.685393" lon="-119.420645">
  <ele>558.385498046875</ele>
  <time>2023-09-15 08:49:22 UTC</time>
  <name>Wire Cache Rest Area</name>
  <desc>Nice rest area with picknick tables, direct access to river (flows really quickly, not for swimming), trash boxes, playground, flush toilets and sink w/water (non potable). Overnight stay is not forbidden, but there is a sign that requests you to limit your stay to 8 hours (no tents though). The highway is very close and noisy &amp; there is a train on the other side of the river that seems to run quite often. In an RV it might be a perfect place for one night, but with a foldable roof, we decided to look for a quieter spot. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-15 08:49:22 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/65278 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
