 <wpt lat="51.222876" lon="-56.776265">
  <ele>44.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-15 18:07:53 UTC</time>
  <name>camp well off the highway</name>
  <desc>A - in parts - rocky gravel road follows the coast for some kilometers. You will find ample camping possibilities, some close to the trees, some on grassy ground, some right at the rocky beach. Very tranquil, inexhaustible fire wood, well away from villages, highway and houses. Access from the Deep Cove Wintering Interpretation Site (signposted 51.2206 -56.7515) or from a turnoff southeast of Anchor Point Village&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-15 18:07:53 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/65537 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
