 <wpt lat="49.440860" lon="-96.980180">
  <ele>216.31671142578125</ele>
  <time>2023-06-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Parc Carillon RV Campground</name>
  <desc>I&#39;ve never actually camped there. I usually just use the &#34;campground&#34; to empty my holding tanks after camping elsewhere. I believe there&#39;s a box to put payment in, or perhaps you&#39;re supposed to pay at the village office down the street. Not too sure on that actually! The entrance is by the &#34;Club Jolys&#34; and is right by the park playground, free splash pad, picnic tables, baseball field, and skateboard park!&#xA;&#xA;According to www.villagestpierrejolys.ca: Whether it&#39;s for visiting family or the community, people with Recreational Vehicles have a place to camp overnight in the Parc Carillon. There are 8 sites. Fee is $20/night.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/65611 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
