  <ele>651.1562269854213</ele>
  <time>2024-07-07 09:51:29 UTC</time>
  <name>Big Thing Creek</name>
  <desc>Big and open space. Several (at least 10) spots on different levels, most with fire rings, some pretty windy. Busy, especially when the Conrad campground is full, but sites here are generously large. Access to water from Big Thing Creek. &#xA;&#xA;There is a popular trail, &#34;Mountain Hero&#34;, which starts right across the Klondike Highway and offers great views of the Windy Arm Lake.&#xA;&#xA;A new foot bridge across the creek allows for easy access to the Conrad Historical Site and the campground.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-07 09:51:29 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/66281 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
