  <name>Adams Lake Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Nice spot at the lake with various sites. CAD 13.-/night and maximum stay is 14 nights. Pit toilets and fire rings. There are also some spaces for tents only and it’s like on a peninsula. &#xA;It’s very quiet at night and very busy during summer. The road is graveled but not bad.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-14 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/66329 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
