 <wpt lat="49.506322" lon="-123.749147">
  <ele>22.68328857421875</ele>
  <time>2023-08-27 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Porpoise Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Like all the provincial parks, this place is in a nice pine forest. The back of the campground adjoins a suburb, so expect lawnmower noise and the sound of people vacuuming.  Kinda weird. But there are sites away from houses.&#xA;This is a good place if you need a safe place to sleep when exploring the area, but there&#39;s nicer and more natural places to be on the sunshine coast.  But they are not always open in off-season.&#xA;Note most of the sites are reservable and fully booked most summers - but there are some first-come first-served sites, plus the operator posts a list of cancellations (available reservable campsites) at some point in the afternoon.&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-27 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Yes&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/66660 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
