 <wpt lat="51.994770" lon="-115.357920">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-04-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>7 Mile Campground</name>
  <desc>Amazing and underused spot! Tons of space; we&#39;ve been there twice now (including a long weekend), and both times only one other group was there.&#xA;&#xA;Operated by the Friends of the Eastern Slopes Association. Annual membership is $30; otherwise, camping is free. &#xA;&#xA;Located close to the Clearwater River. Hiking/biking/horseback riding trails close by. Lots of room in many of the spots for big rigs, toys, horses, etc. Also very tent friendly. &#xA;&#xA;Super clean and well maintained. There are 2 different ways to get to the site; coming from the East/Caroline area is rougher roads with a /lot/ of tight turns. Would suggest coming from the West if you&#39;ve got a big rig.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-04-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/70278 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
