 <wpt lat="49.585970" lon="-124.886610">
  <ele>7.3034245491027825</ele>
  <time>2024-07-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Union Bay Boat Ramp</name>
  <desc>ADMIN NOTE:  You have to be self-contained from October to May because there is not a portapotty onsite in the off season. That means you must have your own toilet and you pack out what you pack in. &#xA;&#xA;ALL Dogs must be on a leash and please pickup and pack out your dogs&#39; poop.&#xA;&#xA;No garbage cans on location. Again pack in pack out.&#xA;&#xA;Two-day maximum stay. If you stay two days in a thirty-day period you’ll be asked not to return for thirty days.&#xA;&#xA;If there is limited room for boaters RVs will be asked to park closer together or in extreme cases asked to leave.&#xA;&#xA;There are Regular checks at the boat launch.&#xA;&#xA;It is unfortunate that we have had to put these guidelines in place but the community area was being abused by a few.&#xA;&#xA;Nice level parking lot beside the water but please park at north end past the ‘parking for boat trailers only’ sign. Have stayed here often and never had a problem. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/71346 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="50.686747" lon="-114.243228">
  <ele>1174.7616844177246</ele>
  <time>2024-07-22 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Lions International Campground Black Diamond</name>
  <desc>Cute place for a one night stop. We had been in the road for a long time and the mom and pop owners were very welcoming and accommodating. Normal price is $40 a night, but we said we didn&#39;t need any services so she gave us a deal at $25. Donna then let us have the bathroom key, access to her collection of DVD&#39;s and music, extra firewood, and even let us plug in a borrow her space heater for the night. The owners are super sweet and it&#39;s a nice quiet place to relax for the night. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-22 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/71352 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
