 <wpt lat="48.392344" lon="-123.943170">
  <ele>24.38448715209961</ele>
  <time>2024-05-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>French beach Provincial park</name>
  <desc>Nice provincial campground and day use area. 5 minutes walk to the beach. Camping in the middle of tall trees!&#xA;Rates are:&#xA;High season: 26$&#xA;Low season: 13$ (after Nov 1st)&#xA;Wood bundle: 8$&#xA;It&#39;s self registration in low season.&#xA;No electricity or water at sites. Water and pit toilet available in close walking distances from each camping spot. The Ranger told me there is a hot shower available close to the group camping (high season only)&#xA;&#xA;Dogs must be on a leash even in your own campground. The park managers threaten eviction at the first offence. If you don’t mind a restrictive camping experience, this is the place for you.&#xA;&#xA;There is a dump station for 5$ with potable water.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/75081 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.337749" lon="-124.739344">
  <ele>119.4869384765625</ele>
  <time>2024-05-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Horne Lake Regional Park</name>
  <desc>A standard regional park campground. $20 for forest site, $24 for lakeside (+tax). Off season (mid-october) is $10 for forest or lakeside site. Nice big flat forested sites, picnic table, fire rings.&#xA;2 bars LTE reception with Bell.&#xA;&#xA;There’s some caves nearby (Horne Lake Caves Provincial Park) while you can take a self guided tour of, definitely recommend. Get a map from the visitor centre.&#xA;&#xA;Lake has beautiful clear water, great for swimming&#xA;&#xA;Currently water has a boil advisory but is typically potable.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/75343 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="50.540290" lon="-126.823748">
  <ele>44.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Forest Campground. Telegraph Grove</name>
  <desc>Over 100 sites, open year round, but with significant closures in winter that may affect your decision to come here between October and March. Fantastic scenery and trails on site. Free hot showers (push button) in the bathrooms. Washrooms closed seasonally. The closest ones in the winter are in Telegraph Cove, a 10-minute walk away. Power adapters (60 amp to 30, etc) are available for a $20 deposit if they have a spare one, which is not guaranteed. Managers say they have never turned anyone away due to lack of space.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/75594 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="51.330930" lon="-117.009109">
  <ele>773.6788209988451</ele>
  <time>2023-09-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Golden Golf RV Park</name>
  <desc>This is the only campground around here which is open even in winter! Nice large sites between trees. (More RV parking in town at the Inns, but they are not nice.) &#xA;With electricity and WiFi at the sites, but no other hook up. No open fires allowed. Water to carry inside the park in summer, in winter at the golf maintenance building.&#xA;Flush toilets in camping area. Need a code to access.&#xA;$45 per night.&#xA;Showers $1,- for four minutes&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/75668 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
