 <wpt lat="45.956697" lon="-62.748671">
  <ele>-16.72637939453125</ele>
  <time>2023-06-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Woodland Islands Ferry Terminal</name>
  <desc>Public car park right next to the ferry terminal where overnight parking is allowed. Particularly good if you are leaving the Northumberland Ferry (turn right just before toll booths) or arriving (turn left after toll booths) Great view to the west. Some noise from ferry workers and arriving vehicles but it is not objectionable. PEI Visitor Center up the road might be better if you want a quieter spot.&#xA;At the ferry terminal, there&#39;s Wi-Fi (not fast), outdoor water tap, some outlets to plug in portables, dog park, and sorting receptacles for recycling and compost. In season, there may be an open snack place at the harbor fishing pier. Beware of mosquitoes and no bathroom access after the terminal closes. &#xA;The nearby Wood Islands Historic Lighthouse (no overnight parking posted) is a good area to visit and walk with lots of green space and a good view of the ferries coming and going.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Yes&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/77425 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
