  <ele>199.0</ele>
  <time>2023-10-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Burnt Beach Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Free provincial rec site. The gravel road in is filled with potholes and the turnoff for Burnt Beach is really narrow, a bit steep. No one else there in the winter, but hunters may be in the area. Locals say that there are a ton of free rec sites by lakes nearby, so the area doesn&#39;t get too filled up in the summer. Pit toilet available. Each site has picnic tables and fire pit. Quaint little private bay.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/78786 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
