  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-04-06 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Pye Point Campsite</name>
  <desc>Absolutely stunning little campsite. It is an official provincial recreation site, so there are 2 picnic tables, a fire ring, and an outhouse. There is even a small dock for swimming, or launching canoes and kayaks.  This is a free site, however it is first come first serve. There are a few other sites around if this one is taken. Accessed via logging roads. About a 15 minute drive off the paved highway.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-04-06 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/83328 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
