  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Esker Lakes Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Provincial Park run by Ontario Parks.&#xA;&#xA;Nice, quite, secluded park with only 100 or so campsites.&#xA;&#xA;Offers full amenities, laundromat, showers, etc.&#xA;&#xA;Great opportunity to view moose, bear and especially partridge. Opportunity to pick and eat wild blueberries in August is an awesome experience.&#xA;&#xA;Campsites start around $40 a night, ~$5 more for electricity.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/84609 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
