 <wpt lat="50.757502" lon="-120.865109">
  <ele>343.5063251173124</ele>
  <time>2024-05-27 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Steelhead Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Small park directly located at the lake. There are hot showers, only for registered campers though. I guess you have to pay a small fee if you want to shower otherwise. Without water and power: 23 CAD. With it was around 30 CAD. Its right at the train tracks in a corner where every train will you his horn... So expect a rather noisy night. Fire pits and benches on every site. Hookup only at around 6 sites. Firewood and ice available. Drinking water directly from town. Very clean toilets. Friendly owner. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-27 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/92726 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
