 <wpt lat="54.318360" lon="-114.732550">
  <ele>611.4</ele>
  <time>2022-10-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Next to Athabasca river </name>
  <desc>Nice, big place directly on the Athabasca River. Some old fire pit. Very quiet. Just some birds and the river :-)&#xA; The place itself is very big. But the acces is very narrow and bumpy. With our van it was no problem, but should be difficult with big RVs. depending on conditions, you would need 4x4 and higher clearance. When it’s raining, it’s getting muddy and you definitely need 4x4! When it’s dry, you can try it with 2wd. &#xA;&#xA;In the curve of the Range Road take the small way into the forest and follow it for about 200m. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-10-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/92809 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
