 <wpt lat="45.226147" lon="-67.191431">
  <ele>13.786954879760742</ele>
  <time>2023-07-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Oak Bay Campground </name>
  <desc>Great little campground we found just after driving across the border into New Brunswick. Owners were super friendly, Park is in great condition. Main park area has serviced sites, 30 amp with sewer and water, well behaved dogs are allowed, and there is great access to the beach for walks at low tide. Main campground area is visible from the road, but traffic noise is not noticeable. There are also some primitive campsites back in the trees a bit if you don’t need services and have a smaller rig. I am here in the early season so I’m sure he gets a lot busier during the summer but, in early May this place is delightful! Not nearly as crowded as the parks closer to, and in St. Andrew. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/93582 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
