  <ele>35.906057316912545</ele>
  <time>2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Pipers Hole River</name>
  <desc>An old abandoned provincial park.  One big lot with some smaller spots as you go down the road. Several locals fish at the river.  Follow the road and you&#39;ll see the oldest bridge in Newfoundland.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/97947 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
