 <wpt lat="60.800691" lon="-137.508852">
  <ele>664.0</ele>
  <time>2024-05-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gravel parking next to quiet road</name>
  <desc>Just a couple of hundred meters off the Highway beyond the Camping Site of Pine Lake.&#xA;There&#39;s a large pull out on the left hand side of the bend before crossing the little lake.&#xA;Quite, some cars passing by during the day.&#xA;Suitable for 2WD lake is accessible for swimming and there&#39;s a natural spring, just before the lake there&#39;s a little gap in the bush that leads you to a tube with springwater.&#xA;&#xA;We heard of bears in the area, didn&#39;t see one, but supposedly there&#39;s a mama grizzly with a cub living in the area west of Pine Lake.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/100708 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
