  <name>Blanket Creek provincial park</name>
  <desc>About 90 sites, mostly all perfectly level. $28 a night which includes unlimited hot showers. Far nicer than staying in Revelstoke as it&#39;s nice and quiet next to the lake. All places in Revelstoke are super loud with highway traffic and trains all through the night. Has a free grey water disposal, and $5 sani dump. can purchase firewood.  Has a man made swimming lagoon and beach. Nice trails and waterfall around campsite&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-15 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/101672 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
