 <wpt lat="45.062225" lon="-79.792692">
  <ele>430.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Moon River </name>
  <desc>Crown land camp area. Wild camping with no amenities.  Good for an overnight stay if you&#39;re travelling. Just off of the highway. Some flat areas for ground tents, good for rig camping,  if you drive in a bit it is 4wd, if you park at the entrance of the trail it is for all size vehicles. A short trail hike to some great fishing. Some locals like to use this spot for a dump at the entrance, just a heads up. Been many times and never been bothered. Hunting season is active here. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/101985 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
