 <wpt lat="44.824588" lon="-81.175955">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-06-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Berford Lake Freshwater Well</name>
  <desc>At Berford Lake Park there is a well that is permanently on, pumping clean, fresh water. There is a sign stating that this water is not tested by the provincial authorities but locals from all over are always coming and filling their water here. Why? Because it’s clean and delicious! The only thing anyone said against it is that it’s hard water with potentially lots of calcium content. (i.e. boiling it could leave scales in your tea kettle)&#xA;&#xA;Not sure of what times of year they turn it on and off. Definitely on in the summertime. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/102012 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Water</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>amenity_drinking_water</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#0099ff</osmand:color>
