 <wpt lat="48.428125" lon="-70.384324">
  <ele>133.2389902185987</ele>
  <time>2023-08-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Rivière Ste-Marguerite #54</name>
  <desc>MODERATOR NOTE: WARNING! Flash floods reported in this location. Please use caution &#xA;&#xA;Reserve and pay 30$/night &#xA;You CANNOT pay on their website.&#xA;You must call 418-236-4604 or 1-877-236-4604&#xA;&#xA;We spoke to the gentleman who is also collecting the money if you did not call and he said he is checking all the spots during the day and every day. He passed by at 5:30pm, then 9:30pm and 8am next morning.&#xA;He told us he is entitled to give fines.&#xA;&#xA;Great spot between the mountains and beside the Ste-Marguerite River. Not too far from the road. On the 172, take the little dirt road with the green #54 sign. Has fire pits, trash can and picnic tables. Fishermen have to register and pay 25$ to camp there, but with about 100 spots like this near the river, there are slim chances that you will see anyone. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/102108 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
