 <wpt lat="48.206783" lon="-84.846880">
  <ele>339.0</ele>
  <time>2024-06-15 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Trans Canada. North of Wawa</name>
  <desc>We came in and stayed the evening with our 26 footer and there was enough room ( with a little bit of wiggle )&#xA;The water, as seen in the third photo, was right out our window through the trees.&#xA;The second picture is taken from the water....the boat launch and it shows our RV on the right with a small back-up entrance at the left and at the top is highway 17...not far away but very quiet due to all the trees.&#xA;A very private spot with room for one more camper a little smaller.&#xA;It was a VERY windy night but it was so well protected we felt almost nothing.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-15 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/103429 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
