 <wpt lat="52.561256" lon="-56.309515">
  <ele>5.784751400794975</ele>
  <time>2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Long Point </name>
  <desc>Amazing camp site. &#xA;Dont be put off by the dump site on the road on the way down. &#xA;A little bumpy but we brought our 38ft fifth wheel nice and slowly. Plenty of room to turn. &#xA;Right on the river, great fishing.&#xA;&#xA;Lots of locals visited the spot after work to fish, we talked to a few, very friendly. &#xA;&#xA;Buy gas at the red roof gas station and she let us fill our water tank too. Even let us leave the trailer while we went for a drive. &#xA;This is a great camp spot before hitting the road to Goose Bay. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Take note where the tide comes too, our rig got completely surrounded by water as we parked right by the wharf in high tide. &#xA;Plenty places on higher ground. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/104999 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
