 <wpt lat="60.263476" lon="-135.068122">
  <ele>863.7722364299052</ele>
  <time>2023-06-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Wheaton River Pullout </name>
  <desc>Abandoned gold mine road, wilderness getaway. Down a long well-maintained gravel road, over two bridges onto a non-maintained gravel road. &#xA;After the second bridge, another 1km or so, and a few places come up on the right alongside the river. &#xA;Plenty of room for any size rig but the track is bumpy so it&#39;s slow after the second bridge. &#xA;Once you have your spot, you can disconnect your tow vehicle, TOAD or even better ATV and follow the track a further 10k or so right up into the mountains to explore closed but recent gold mines and the mining camp. &#xA;&#xA;Camping spot alone is worth the journey, very peaceful and 360 views of mountains. &#xA;A few locals came by but not much and all were friendly. &#xA;We visited with a 38ft fifth wheel, roughly 9 tonnes. I reckon the second bridge will be good for 20 to 30 tonnes. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/105015 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="63.919476" lon="-139.315557">
  <ele>492.36265418608514</ele>
  <time>2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gold Panning Area</name>
  <desc>50m or so from the area you can legally search for your own gold. &#xA;&#xA;Road is good, plenty of space for any configuration of rig or tent. Probably fit 6 or so big rigs easily.&#xA;&#xA;Pan for gold in to the evening to your hearts content, who knows you could leave this spot a millionaire!&#xA;&#xA;Couple fire pits here already, I chatted to a guy who has been here 3 nights and had no problem. I also asked a local and he said its no problem.&#xA;Gold mining activity happening all around this spot, really cool to see. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/105016 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
