 <wpt lat="46.531001" lon="-84.251538">
  <ele>160.26787929095036</ele>
  <time>2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Husky/Esso 24/7 Truck Stop</name>
  <desc>Another Husky Truck stop / Travel center&#xA;&#xA;This places are amazing!&#xA;Located from BC (Chilliwack) to Ontario (Kingston) close to the main Highways.&#xA;Recognizable by a huuuge Canadian Flag next to it.&#xA;Shop (with toilets, laundromat and showers) is open 24/7.&#xA;Also have a restaurant and usually free wifi (not always tho).&#xA;&#xA;Before you use the showers: go to the counter, sign up for a husky rewards card, download the app and subscribe to the newsletter. &#xA;You instantly get 200 rewards points only for that! &#xA;Also you can find other Husky Truck Stops / Travel Centers with the app!&#xA;&#xA;A shower (if you bring your own towl) is only 50 points (or ~8$)! &#xA;(If you need a towel it is 100 points or ~10$).&#xA;&#xA;The showers are AMAZING!&#xA;Super clean, you have no time limit and get a whole private bathroom. (You can even bring your phone and powerbank in to charge meanwhile).&#xA;&#xA;Laundry is usually coin system and around 1,25$ for washing and 1,25$ for dryer (1h).&#xA;&#xA;Even tho it is no problem, I would not recommend to sleep here (as it gets very loud next to the street and because some truckers leave their engine running the whole night).&#xA;&#xA;Big rigs would fit, places are meant for the truckers tho!! No problem for small vehicles.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - Not at Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/106006 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
