 <wpt lat="50.146480" lon="-115.804550">
  <ele>801.0</ele>
  <time>2024-05-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kootenay River</name>
  <desc>You can reach this spot with a small van or maybe with a car if it has enough clearance. There are many spots along the river shore of the Kootenay River.&#xA;&#xA;In the evening, locals were here and had a fire but the spot is wide.&#xA;&#xA;Cell phone signal is a bit weak but functional with my provider (bell/virgine)&#xA;&#xA;To access the spot, take the dirt road on the north side of the bridge.&#xA;&#xA;When you get close to the river, if you don&#39;t have a 4x4, follow the dirt road on your right. A little bit further, you can access the river and choose your spot.&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/106078 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
