 <wpt lat="57.226084" lon="-122.702570">
  <ele>939.8381752229062</ele>
  <time>2024-07-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Old Alaska Highway</name>
  <desc>A good place to camp - close to the highway but completely out of sight behind a dirt wall and forest. Compact gravel, clean, no infrastructure, space for several small campers/cars. Follow the track (starts to overgrow) down for approx. 400-500 meters, no 4x4 needed. watch out for mud. And we had NO bugs/mosquitoes.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/106290 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
