 <wpt lat="45.652530" lon="-60.872060">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-10-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>St-Peters National Historic Site</name>
  <desc>This is opposite to Battery Provincial Park on the other side of the canal.&#xA;I guess we could have stayed on the parking down the hill near the water (and actually on the St-Peters National Historic Site), but we did not feel comfortable. We instead climb up the hill and found this small dirt and grassy parking near the St-Peters Coastal Trail.&#xA;In theory, we would have a nice view on the water from this higher point, but bushes and small trees obstruct the view, at least from the RV. You can walk to the edge of the hill though to get a nice view.&#xA;It was quiet. There was another RV (kind of a 4x4 high clearance monster RV) when we were there, but nobody in it.&#xA;We were in a camper van. It is not big-rig-friendly, but I guess a small trailer could stay there as well.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/107350 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
