 <wpt lat="49.859270" lon="-93.772704">
  <ele>448.5071913515723</ele>
  <time>2022-08-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Medicine Lake</name>
  <desc>Medicine Lake is set back from route 17 behind George lake.  The access road to Medicine Lake is a 2 lane oiled and well traveled road easily traveled by a big rig.  Medicine lake access road 2 leads to a large solid  gravel area in which a big rig can turn around in. It has multiple fire rings and appears to be an area that locals use for fishing access and ATV play. There is evidence of camping, but no one was here when we arrived. There are many mosquitoes. We heard boats on the lake until sunset and there was light road noise from the highway. No signs about camping or anything else.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/107583 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
