 <wpt lat="50.759361" lon="-119.165866">
  <ele>1145.0</ele>
  <time>2024-05-31 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Amazing view of Shuswap Lake on Larch Hill</name>
  <desc>Amazing site up the forest service road. Road is actively used for recreation and biking, so is in good shape. Very little road traffic at this point though. No amenities. Decent signal. Extremely quiet. Infinite fire wood. Out of the way and therefore private. We had C-Class camper up these steepish roads just fine. Big 5th wheelers may struggle on a few hairpin turns. Once arrived, area is flat, spacious and beautiful views. Not windy when we were here, but could possibly get windy somedays as it&#39;s a cleared area.&#xA;BEST LOOKOUT OVER THE SHUSWAP LAKE. WORTH THE DRIVE UP.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-31 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/107595 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
