 <wpt lat="55.196103" lon="-129.116791">
  <ele>55.266651287736906</ele>
  <time>2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Provincial park campsite</name>
  <desc>Situated in the middle of the lava fields this campsite offers close proximity to both the lava (surrounded by) and the Higu Isgwit hot springs (about 10 miles away). This campsite is self registration for the sum of $20 a night. It offers forested individual areas with picnic table and fire pit in each. Nice area, hardly anyone here when we stayed. &#xA;Can’t be sure if potable water but there is a well hand pump ant pit toilets . &#xA;Be aware: We had been parked in a local parking area close by but was moved on by park official to this site. We hadn’t realised we were within the park ! &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/108993 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
