 <wpt lat="65.650195" lon="-138.135454">
  <ele>502.1438463222527</ele>
  <time>2023-08-01 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Little Bear Lake</name>
  <desc>Found by coincidence by simply driving a little road beside the Dempster Highway for cooking lunch on our way to Inuvik. &#xA;Seems like sometimes some people stop here, there was a little fire ring.&#xA;The way ends after maybe 70 meters at a nice spot near some little lakes (I tried to catch fish there, but unsuccessful).&#xA;There were many  footprints of bears, different sizes from big to small, black bears and Grizzlys. Also traces of other animals like moose and Elk, I think. &#xA;Pretty place, be bear aware and I think it’s a good stop around the 230 km mark of Dempster Highway for preparing lunch, but also for a night or 2. &#xA;No facilities here, just pure nature. Please keep that place clean.&#xA;&#xA;Room for 1 vehicle, not rec for large rvs, very tight turning circle. We were comfortable with our 21ft b class or if your bigger reverse in. Road in is wide and clear of overhang trees, Short 50meters from the road behind thick established trees for privacy, right on the lake with a friendly beaver as a neighbour. Unsealed, gravel road which was easy to drive even after snow. Mostly flat so room for a tent. Beautiful lake and mountain views&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-01 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/109639 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
