 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="46.367943" lon="-62.135783">
  <ele>6.297339409612128</ele>
  <time>2023-08-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Red Point provincial park, PE</name>
  <desc>We came here on the off season so not sure when the season opens. But we stayed here for free, it’s an actual campground in the summer season, it looks like but doesn’t look like it gets much action after summer time. Great for tenting, RV, and everything basically. We were lucky we had running water at this area on one of the sinks that are outside but the other areas water was shut off. Easy stair access to the beach and lots of picnic tables. And the view was amazing! Had a couple cars drive through no visitors, and no one bothered us. Very quiet.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/112048 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="47.980597" lon="-84.785395">
  <ele>266.51055556628853</ele>
  <time>2023-07-01 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Water Reservoir Access Road</name>
  <desc>Public access road that goes around the town&#39;s water reservoir. It is wooded on both sides so it&#39;s dark, being an untraveled access road there isn&#39;t any traffic, its far enough from the town and the highway to be quiet, and it is very wide so vehicles of all sizes can easily park here. Big rigs can pull in from one side and drive straight out the other.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-01 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/112058 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
