 <wpt lat="49.309204" lon="-122.324045">
  <ele>63.66917970460594</ele>
  <time>2023-10-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Bottom of Stave Lake</name>
  <desc>Dispersed camping on the sandy, dry bottom of an arm of Stave Lake. It&#39;s popular with quads, SxSs and off-roaders, especially on weekends. Might be flooded in spring and early summer.&#xA;Lots of room to choose from, avoid the muddy puddles and the old bonfires. &#xA;Access from the Rocky Point FSR and from the far end of Rocky Point Rec Site.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/112852 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
