 <wpt lat="49.737222" lon="-125.295903">
  <ele>1097.2928547980264</ele>
  <time>2024-01-17 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Mt Washington Ski Car Park (lower) </name>
  <desc>The upper car parks of the ski resort are all are strictly no overnight parking. Down here there is a small &#39;no overnight parking&#39; sign in the corner, but we asked and were told by staff that it is OK for RVs to park overnight. Huge level car park, lots of space for any size rig. Several other RVs were here with us for 5 nights and nobody said anything. There is a ski-lift by the car-park, so you can ski in/out to your RV, or you can drive the short distance up the hill to the main centre during the day. Beware on Mon-Weds the ski lifts stop at 15:30hrs!!&#xA;There were some portaloos in the corner of the car park (but not sure whether they are there all the time) otherwise no facilities. Free. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-01-17 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/128828 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.199912" lon="-96.894140">
  <ele>275.79923357879375</ele>
  <time>2023-05-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>The Cliff</name>
  <desc>This spot is located south of Winnipeg, south of Roseau. Great spot to stop if you are heading south or want to explore a little. &#xA;Small area and cliff off the Roseau River. &#xA;It’s located on/next to the crow wing trail at the end of the road and an entrance. No signs forbid staying overnight only to respect the area as this trail travels from southern Manitoba to Winnipeg crossing some private property. It was used in the early 1900’s. Follow the boat dock trail down if you have 4x4 and you will find a spot on the river. &#xA;I’m a local and don’t think you should have a problem staying here. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-05-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/129000 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
