 <wpt lat="49.871201" lon="-123.251204">
  <ele>0.03179931640625</ele>
  <time>2023-08-26 02:28:53 UTC</time>
  <name>Squamish Valley Campground </name>
  <desc>Rustic &amp; VERY expensive camping alongside the Squamish River. No facilities other than pit toilets. Fees are $15/per person, + $5/vehicle, + $5/ dog. Fees are for each individual person, and not for the campsite. We paid $45/day for one rustic campsite per night for 2 people in a camper vanc(+ 1 dog), with no facilities and not even on riverside! Most expensive dry camping &amp; run down site that I&#39;ve visited throughout N. America! &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-26 02:28:53 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/129598 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
