  <ele>595.8525390625</ele>
  <time>2024-07-02 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Noble canyon road</name>
  <desc>Wild camping recommended by some locals along a gravel road (government lands). FREE. The road is bumpy but accessible even for big rigs. You can Park anywhere on the side of the road but there is an unofficial spot after 3 bridges next to a creek, like 5mn drive from the highway. We didnt go further but there is probably other spots along the road. A lot of locals come here in the day for using their quads and motocross &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-02 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/133290 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
