 <wpt lat="53.871717" lon="-122.284767">
  <ele>755.2</ele>
  <time>2023-07-22 09:21:37 UTC</time>
  <name>Willow River Recreation Site, Staging area #5</name>
  <desc>There are several areas in the immediate vicinity to camp. We exited the highway on the West side of the bridge turning South. We then drove for over a mile, bearing left at each of the two Y’s and came to this spot. The end of the road is a very large cul-de-sac capable of working with any vehicle. There are a lot of pot holes on the gravel road so be forewarned. There is a path down to the river and according to the info board this is the take out area for kayakers.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-22 09:21:37 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/133391 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
