  <name>Island Lake Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>A pretty, first-come, first-serve campground on a small lake just off Highway 3 near Crowsnest Pass.&#xA;Facilities include fire rings, picnic tables, a boat launch and a pit toilet outhouse.&#xA;23 dollars a night. Maximum stay is 16 nights. the downside is you are between Highway 3 and the railroad tracks.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-14 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/134036 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
