 <wpt lat="45.722905" lon="-62.653684">
  <ele>21.95156478881836</ele>
  <time>2023-06-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Caribou-Munroes Island Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Standard provincial park. Smaller camping places are among the trees, very sheltered. So also many mosquitoes (there are roofed shelters, but they have no screens). The field for bigger rigs is open and has a look over the bay. Reasonably priced CAD 26.70 for tent plus 1 person. The Picknick area has a beautiful view over said bay. Wifi only at reception. Weak cell signal.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/134180 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
