 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="60.598533" lon="-134.850927">
  <ele>750.0</ele>
  <time>2023-11-17 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Yukon Motorcycle Park</name>
  <desc>Every motorcyclist should include this spot in their trip north or south, whatever, come here. There’s a workshop for maintenance, hot showers, power, wifi, washing machines and a pub with great food and beer. Campfires most nights. You’ll get lots of up-to-date info about the area here. &#xA;&#xA;Campsites are $25 (i think) and there’s glamping tents for $70 (I think), these are a great option for pairs or couples. So much better than setting up your tent and blow-up mattress, especially if there’s poor weather.&#xA;&#xA;I doubt bookings are necessary as they’ve built so many sites and tents, maybe a good idea for glamping tents in peak season.&#xA;&#xA;And the owners are full of local knowledge to help you solve anything that may come up.&#xA;&#xA;If you need parts sent in advance, send them an email for their post box address. Good luck getting tires and getting them fitted in Whitehorse if you haven’t ordered/booked in advance. You can maybe buy them in town, maybe they’re quiet enough to fit them - or order them online to here and fit them in the workshop.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-11-17 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/134241 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="52.259242" lon="-106.781830">
  <ele>493.04368923657137</ele>
  <time>2023-07-11 23:16:08 UTC</time>
  <name>Campland RV Park</name>
  <desc>This is the best campground! The staff is super friendly and the place is pretts new. Bathrooms and showers are super clean and modern. ($2 for shower). We stayed here two nights. It is very close to Saskatoon and you can hear the highway but it didn&#39;t bother us. Paid about $30 per night.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-11 23:16:08 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Fast&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/134248 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
