 <wpt lat="50.315579" lon="-126.030194">
  <ele>265.919189453125</ele>
  <time>2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Keta Lake Rest Area</name>
  <desc>We were heading north on the Saturday of a long weekend.  All camp sites full so enroute to Elk River Rest Area (in 20 km) we came across this one and stopped. No &#39;no overnight parking/camping&#39; signs.  Picnic tables, pit clean pit toilets, trash bins and level pavement.  There is a grassy area between lot and lake but not sure if tents would be allowed.  There is a trail to the lake but not a great access or view.  No cell reception.  Quiet from dusk to dawn.  No one bothered us.  &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/136500 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
