 <wpt lat="48.827642" lon="-125.130271">
  <ele>19.47981834411621</ele>
  <time>2024-04-16 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Centennial Municipal Campground</name>
  <desc>Nice campground in Bamfield offered by the local community. 14 places for RV’s with firepits and separate places for tents. Flush toilets and showers behind the office building.&#xA;Roads in Bamfield are paved, but the 80km dirt road from Port Alberni is not in a perfect state. Can be done with a 2 wheel drive, only when doing very slow.&#xA;Not recommended for big RV’s or big trailers.&#xA;Bamfield is a very nice town at the end of the West Coast Trail and has beautiful beaches and marine wildlife spotting.&#xA;Worth the detour!!&#xA;$25 per night, $5 for firewood.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-04-16 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/138032 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
