 <wpt lat="45.949689" lon="-79.487485">
  <ele>136.3</ele>
  <time>2024-07-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Crown Land Camping</name>
  <desc>The coordinates will take you to the entrance.  &#xA;&#xA;This is crown land, about 30 minutes from Resoule Provincial Park.&#xA;&#xA;At the end of this&#34;drive way&#34; is the camp site. There isn&#39;t much of a turn around so if you have something bigger than a pickup truck, I suggest you just back in or find a different spot. &#xA;&#xA;There is only space for one rig, unless you are traveling with friends then you can park in tandem.&#xA;&#xA;There is a bit of mud, I wouldn&#39;t suggest parking anything big here if it is wet.&#xA;&#xA;If this spot is taken, try the next entrance which is just 10 seconds to the West. (I didn&#39;t investigate the other site but it looked similar on Google maps.)&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/138295 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
