 <wpt lat="49.801050" lon="-126.411835">
  <ele>11.101727281204518</ele>
  <time>2024-06-07 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Conuma river rec site</name>
  <desc>couple of sites right on the river.       we had a black bear and eagle fishing on the river right in front of us, very nice entertainment since it was pouring rain.   Also had a seal swimming upriver. We got in easily with our 22 foot C class.&#xA;A word of caution. We arrived just after the rain started and camped about 50 feet from the 20 foot wide calm stream. It took about 2 hours for the stream to get to a 200 ft wide torrent within about 10 feet of our MH. While it never appeared that the site would flood, we would recommend keeping an eye on the water level during and after rain events.&#xA;We added two pictures of the river so you can see the difference in the river after all the rain.&#xA;Came back in the afternoon, the place had flooded after two days of solid and hard rain.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-07 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/138353 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
