 <wpt lat="50.703846" lon="-127.861838">
  <ele>194.4313942519948</ele>
  <time>2023-05-16 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Nahwitti Lake Rec Site </name>
  <desc>It’s a long drive in down a logging road so beware of that, but very quiet spot. Small spots, our van (16 ft long, 8ft wide) is about as big as you can fit here. There doesn’t seem to be a fee, no sign and no attendant. All sites are equipped with fire pit and picnic tables. It’s a good half way spot between Port Hardy and Cape Scott Provoncial Park. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-05-16 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/139127 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
