 <wpt lat="61.621340" lon="-135.882420">
  <ele>652.4896809253455</ele>
  <time>2024-04-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Roadside</name>
  <desc>Driving north in Yukon, I did not like the open gravel area to the south so I kept driving a few miles/kilometers passed Braeburn, where a sign showed a “photo rest stop.”  Across the road from this stop is a gravel road that leads to an incredible open area. It is near a creek so I listened to running water all night. There are fire rings. The road is near, but rather than being a nuisance, it actually provided comfort because this place feels like I’m in the “nature of Yukon!!” &#xA;I highly recommend this place to travelers in the area if you’re looking to park for a night. It was great to me anyway. &#xA;Cheers all!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-04-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/143424 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
