 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="48.181000" lon="-77.721000">
  <ele>295.6559905390083</ele>
  <time>2024-07-05 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Lac des Soeurs</name>
  <desc>On the shores of Lac des Sœurs, a large car park that is very easy to access for all types of vehicles. Small beach for swimming, walking path in the forest. A few shaded areas for camping. Popular place, family but remains rather quiet. Sorry no photo, but ask google.&#xA;--&#xA;Au bord du lac des Sœurs, grand parking très facile d&#39;accès pour tout type de véhicule. Petite plage pour baignade, chemin de promenade dans la forêt. Quelques coin ombragés pour camper. Endroit fréquenté, familial mais reste plutôt calme. Pas de photo désolé,.mais demande à Google.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-05 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/145737 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.010720" lon="-117.553152">
  <ele>446.46112060546875</ele>
  <time>2024-05-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Pend D&#39;Oreille Reservoir</name>
  <desc>Beautiful roadside pull off.  A rough but 2wd doable road leads down away from the highway to a flat-ish area with a beach (when the water&#39;s low) and fire ring.&#xA;The spot is highly visited by locals, many of them fishing or putting their boats in the water, but all of them are friendly and few people stay the night.  We were always alone after 8:30.  &#xA;Groundhogs, ducks, and wild Canadian Geese (not the city park variety) are plenty, and there&#39;s a beautiful waterfall on the cliff opposite the campsite.&#xA;BW AWARE, we were here in March/April and the ticks were AWFUL!  Be sure to check yourself any time you go for a hike.  We picked several (10+) off our clothes after a hike in the woods.  On the plus side, there&#39;s tons of dry wood in the forest for campfires.&#xA;&#xA;Enjoy, clean up after yourself, and be safe!&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/145809 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.047023" lon="-117.294094">
  <ele>585.28173828125</ele>
  <time>2024-07-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Large Open Space on Salmon River</name>
  <desc>The small dirt road heading down to this spot is on the West side of Highway 6, which connects Nelway to Salmo.  The road is 2wd capable, and not much clearance is needed, a small car might be a bit of a challenge, but I think it is entirely doable.  The spot is wide open, with lots of space for many large campers.  If you continue driving past the clearing there are a few prospectors camps, and there is a sandy beach right by the river with a fire pit.  &#xA;&#xA;The river is swift in April and we used the water for coffee.  BC water is pretty pure, so a 1 minute boil should assure you clear, safe drinking water.&#xA;&#xA;Road noise is minimal during the day, and the nights are super quiet.  &#xA;&#xA;The area was clean, so please pack all your stuff out.&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/145810 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
