 <wpt lat="51.272830" lon="-115.049930">
  <ele>1537.34423828125</ele>
  <time>2022-08-27 15:58:38 UTC</time>
  <name>Crown Land</name>
  <desc>Another campsite in the PLUZ (public land use zone aka crown land). Whole stretch of road is crown land and seemingly popular. Tons of camp sites available year-round. This one has trees cleared away (great for charging solar panels), and an amazing view of the mountains. Some of the campsites are close together (meaning neighbours are close), but this one is pretty big (could fit two or three vans if traveling together). Great cell service. Came here on a Wednesday at the beginning of May and a lot of the sites closer to the entrance of the PLUZ were already occupied.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-27 15:58:38 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/149670 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
