 <wpt lat="50.020420" lon="-120.637560">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-26 08:25:57 UTC</time>
  <name>Kane Valley Trails </name>
  <desc>This is a grass-covered, old rustic parking lot designed for snowmobilers and horseback riders to park.  I don&#39;t think it&#39;s used much, if at all.  There is an old pit toilet at the edge of the &#34;lot;&#34; however, I didn&#39;t even open the door.&#xA;This is a great place to spend the night if the local campsites/recreational sites are full and you still want to fish.  Spend the night here and then drive into the day-use area of your local favorite lake.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-26 08:25:57 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/150685 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
