 <wpt lat="53.589690" lon="-110.431620">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-01 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Vermillion River</name>
  <desc>A nice open, free camping spot or day use area along the Vermilion River with no stay limit. There are pit toilets but they aren&#39;t maintained very well (this may be just now with Covid) and there are garbage containers. Camping is available near the camp kitchen and also in the big open area to the east of the kitchen, close to the river., with a few spots in the trees. Any size rig will fit. It&#39;s right on Hwy 45 northeast of Vermilion Alberta, just a bit east of Dewberry Alberta. I get 1-2 bars of LTE with Telus.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-01 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151033 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
