 <wpt lat="49.499320" lon="-82.762423">
  <ele>247.9</ele>
  <time>2023-05-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gas Line Side Road</name>
  <desc>Small access area just off a gas line access road. We drove down the gravel road until it turned east and then backed onto the small siding area almost in the centre of the gas line clearing. &#xA;&#xA;The gravel side road is in good condition and there is room for one or two units here. There is also some room down the road a little further beside the trees of to the side of the road. &#xA;&#xA;The highway is quite a ways away and you can barely hear the traffic. We sat outside with our fire ring and enjoyed the sunset.  If you were tenting, there are many places to pitch in the grass. We are driving a truck and camper pulling a cargo trailer and had no issues with space. &#xA;&#xA;A local did stop in to let us know that they had seen bears in the area and to be bear-aware with our food and belongings.&#xA;&#xA;Three bars of LTE cell service. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-05-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151084 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.708369" lon="-87.290569">
  <ele>465.2</ele>
  <time>2023-09-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Turkey Lake shore</name>
  <desc>A great spot but popular with the locals. There are multiple sites here that are large enough to for pretty much everything, unless they are taken...  big rigs (class A) might have issues turning around if others are here.  We arrived on a Friday and there were two units already here, both 28-30ft RV trailers pulled by 4x4 pickups. We took a lakeside site with our truck and camper pulling a 20 ft trailer and there were two other sites about the same size. &#xA;There are fire rings and a rocky beach at this location and one of the locals told me there is another area further down the road by the lake with a sandy beach that is usually used by “Jeeps”. &#xA;We could have stayed here a few nights, or maybe even a week but we did not have time. &#xA;NO highway noise at all, just the sound of waves against the shoreline and the loons on the lake. Spotty cell service with only one bar, but you had to be close to the lake to get it. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151178 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
