 <wpt lat="53.381740" lon="-117.655010">
  <ele>958.9</ele>
  <time>2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Athabaska River</name>
  <desc>The main route here is very rut-y, so strongly recommended high clearance only.  Turn right when you see a sign indicating left for the designated camping area.  I&#39;m in a stock Tundra pickup.&#xA;&#xA;I was thinking of turning back early on because the road isn&#39;t fun. but my perseverance paid off.&#xA;&#xA;As you can see, this spot is right by the river.  You could even launch a boat. It is very tight and a bit sandy, so I highly recommend 4wd or AWD.  I had to use it!&#xA;&#xA; Easier, however, and adjacent to his spot, there are 3 or 4 other spots that are very very close and aren&#39;t nearly as tight. They are on a slight hill maybe 4 metre high but you can still walk down to the river.&#xA;&#xA;Big rigs, trailers - don&#39;t bother, you will have trouble on the main road.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151337 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
