 <wpt lat="49.718565" lon="-94.946785">
  <ele>379.4</ele>
  <time>2024-07-23 00:50:49 UTC</time>
  <name>Rush Bay Rd</name>
  <desc>Great spot for an overnight. &#xA;Large wide open area that may have previously been a gravel/sand pit. There are a few places to park and also a decent road that leads into the bush a ways to a large grassy area, about another 100 meters away. &#xA;&#xA;The site is exposed to the small road but quite a ways from the Trans-Canada highway, so you can barely hear the large transport trucks. The side road heading from the highway is paved. The site we parked at was crushed gravel but there are other areas of sand and dirt. &#xA;&#xA;Three bars of LTE. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-23 00:50:49 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151424 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
