 <wpt lat="55.350482" lon="-115.040037">
  <ele>720.2360332014575</ele>
  <time>2023-07-11 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gravel Pit with View</name>
  <desc>This is a large gravel pit area a short distance off the highway. &#xA;There are LOTS of various places to park here for an overnight. &#xA;&#xA;It appears the locals use it for dirt biking and atv’ing and someone has dumped some garbage here in one area. &#xA;&#xA;The roads continue in different directions but we did not explore. &#xA;The road coming in was rough with some ruts but we made it in 2wd in our truck and camper towing a 20ft enclosed cargo trailer. Big class A’s might have issues but a truck and travel trailer should be fine.  If the side road is wet, it may cause issues so be aware. &#xA;&#xA;Very peaceful here with a partial view of the lake. &#xA;NO ROAD noise or train tracks close by. &#xA;One bar of LTE on Bell. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-11 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151702 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
