 <wpt lat="51.097837" lon="-115.064045">
  <ele>1276.6</ele>
  <time>2024-03-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Seebe dam</name>
  <desc>This is a decent spot that&#39;s partially hidden from view.&#xA;There is extreme road noise as well as noise from passing trains who blast their horns multiple times.&#xA;There is no indication of who this land belongs to but no signs forbidding parking camping etc. However I would not set up lawn chairs barbecue etc and just enjoy the spot overnight and possibly a lunch or something as it is not well camouflaged.&#xA;The site is suitable for pickups vans and conversion vans but there is no space to maneuver for class A or trailers.&#xA;I&#39;d say there&#39;s space for about 2 to 3 people.&#xA;This should go without saying that fires would be a dead giveaway so please don&#39;t.&#xA;There also appears to be a boat launch.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-03-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151835 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
