 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="44.615500" lon="-78.013360">
  <ele>213.6293772266964</ele>
  <time>2024-05-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Trailhead parking area for ATV/Snowmobiles</name>
  <desc>LOADS of space, enough for many Class A&#39;s, drive thru. There is a turn around at the mine up the 6 if you pass it. There is better access to the area from the north side which will enable a drive out south, or you will need to exit north to the mine to turn around if entering from the south as the north entrance is too sharp to exit and go south from. Quiet, despite large trucks passing by, sheltered from the road by the bank and trees, wetlands beside for beaver sightings. Be sure to park well off the drive area to allow those using the area to park trucks and trailers, and there is room for 3 abreast at its narrowest point.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/151863 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
