 <wpt lat="49.616333" lon="-95.982556">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Sandilands on the River</name>
  <desc>Accessible from a turnoff on the TransCanada highway in Hadashville (see photo). Gravel roads are a bit rough but doable even in a small vehicle, The roads will lead you to a few campsites on an open hill facing Whitemouth River. There are fire pits. Stars are lovely, beavers in the water, lots of big harmless flies, less mosquitos but still around. Saw many fireflies and even an owl. Quite quiet, try not to leave your car doors open too long because the flies kept getting stuck. Didn’t access the river for water, but it seemed to be a long walk away down the hillside.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/153437 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
