 <wpt lat="49.912066" lon="-126.638237">
  <ele>0.580078125</ele>
  <time>2024-03-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Pete&#39;s farm</name>
  <desc>We found a pull-off from the main road and followed it down a trail. as we drove down we saw a few signs that indicated that at one time this was probably someone&#39;s property. the home is now destroyed but there are a few signs and benches left.&#xA;&#xA;if you follow what we think was an old boat launch down the pebble road, you&#39;ll come to an area on the river that is crystal clear and incredibly shallow! it&#39;s (slow) moving water and suitable for filling a water tank.&#xA;&#xA;this place is incredible. if you choose to use it, please treat it with respect. across the river is the reiner river trail. Tahsis town has cell coverage as well as garbage and recycling. as its economy is struggling (but has some great tourism options), it would be great to have lunch or do a tour while in the area. &#xA;&#xA;wolves are present in this area.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-03-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/154119 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
