 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="46.519478" lon="-80.939970">
  <ele>266.5520608751103</ele>
  <time>2023-08-06 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Canadian Tire</name>
  <desc>Much larger back parking lot and less activity than the other Canadian tire. Better for bigger rigs or those towing as well as small vehicles. Toilets inside during operating hours. Groceries and LCBO close by. Short walk for Tim’s or Walmart wifi. Very bright parking lot lights but should be fine if you have window coverings. Little walking path along creek, probably good for pets. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-06 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/154463 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="53.567885" lon="-116.733805">
  <ele>940.238037109375</ele>
  <time>2024-06-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gravel pit, Miller&#39;s Pond</name>
  <desc>large old gravel pit, with open areas and trees for shade. right off highway 16 west of Edson,AB and before Marlboro. It is an active haul road going in. User maintained. Locals use this area for camping for ATV riding in surrounding forests. large enough for A class motorhomes and C class but I would suggest they stick to the more open areas where road is smoother, or right by the pond. No services, should have a self contained RV. great for an overnight or 2 week stay. We&#39;ve stayed here before and have never had troubles at night with noise.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/154539 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="51.234036" lon="-118.217898">
  <ele>573.2685546875</ele>
  <time>2024-07-15 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Waterside spot</name>
  <desc>Really nice site right on the water. Take a sharp left onto a paved road and there are a few spots early on the right. Keep going to reach a clearing just past a stream with space for 3 campsites or so, reasonably level and with fire pits. One trailer that looks like its here permanently but we didn&#39;t see anyone in it &#xA;&#xA;There were a couple of big rigs while we were here parked on the road as it&#39;s so close to the water. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-15 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/154545 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
