 <wpt lat="53.291664" lon="-60.311340">
  <ele>5.448560797455727</ele>
  <time>2024-07-05 19:51:38 UTC</time>
  <name>Birch Island</name>
  <desc>This area is the site of the old town of Birch Island. It is now a conservation area. From Happy Valley main road, turn right at the El Greco restaurant. Continue to drive until the end of the road. Go under the big gate and cross the bridge (no sign about the maximum weight). Here is the parking with a nice view of the Churchill Falls River. &#xA;On Saturday night, some locals came. A security guard car came a couple of times to check the place. They didn’t say anything. &#xA;In this place you will find picnic table (some are covered), garbage and trails. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-05 19:51:38 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/154641 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
