 <wpt lat="50.517496" lon="-127.021167">
  <ele>36.28511929232627</ele>
  <time>2024-07-16 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kipala Road</name>
  <desc>It’s a 20-30 min drive off HWY 19 down Kipala Main FSR **only 5 mins on FSR if you get on it off hwy 19, coming from the south** and you hit the large bridge going over the Nimpkish river. it’s on the left. A small narrow road leading to the shoreline of where the river meets the lake. It’s absolutely beautiful. The lake is quite windy so you get to hear the lake waves all night :) quiet and desolate,  no-one around and you actually get **some** cell reception! &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-16 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/155825 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
