 <wpt lat="47.063895" lon="-70.452939">
  <ele>0.520416259765625</ele>
  <time>2024-06-29 10:08:33 UTC</time>
  <name>Halte-repos Moulin Vincelotte</name>
  <desc>This quiet campsite situated on the south shore of the St. Lawrence River gives a splendid view of the mountain range on the North shore. 17th century historical windmill on-site. Certain amenities can be found in the close-by town of Cap-St-Ignace such as a grocery store (Bonichoix), a bank/ATM (Desjardins), a petrol station (Petro-Canada) and a drug store (Uniprix).&#xA;&#xA;Price: $35 for trailers $10 for tents &#xA;Note: Funds raised through contributions will allow the property owners to perform renovations and maintain the historical landmark located on site. &#xA;&#xA;No reservations. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-29 10:08:33 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/157593 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
