  <name>Buckhorn, Ontario </name>
  <desc>Sunset crescent on the bottom of the locks at the end of the road , &#xA;small parking lot, some vehicles with empty boat trailers along the edge but we found a spot and it emptied in the evening &#xA;Rest room up the hill at the controls of the locks hrs vary &#xA;Along side of Hwy 36 &#xA;Restaurant up on other side of bridge / lock a walk but not bad &#xA;&#xA;Tent camping allowed if you want to pay for it through the boat lock system. They charge a minimum around 15$ and you get a code for the washrooms. (After hours seems like no one checks, just no washrooms) &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-06 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/158075 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
