  <ele>208.5</ele>
  <time>2023-05-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Small grove by Loss Creek</name>
  <desc>Beautiful spot on the creek, a fair way up the FSR, easy access to the water and there’s a fire pit in place.&#xA;We were heading to the Loss Creek camping spot right on the highway and decided to go up this road instead.&#xA;There are multiple beautiful spots along the road, and right before this spot there is a large opening with space for multiple RV’s or campers. You could fit a big rig in no problem if you’re happy to go down a bit of a rough road.&#xA;The spot we stayed in only has one space but if  it’s free it’s well worth parking up.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-05-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/158299 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
