 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.760813" lon="-92.835649">
  <ele>375.140592825599</ele>
  <time>2023-07-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Nature’s Inn RV and Marina</name>
  <desc>Simple RV and tenting park on the shores of Wabigoon Lake. Stopped here because HWY 17 was closed all day due to a collision. The couple that operate the park are nice. Facilities (shower and toilet) are quite old and dated, but clean enough. Paid $25 cash for a tent site for our campervan (no site services), which provided a great view of the lake. Sign in bathroom says sink water must be boiled before drinking - not sure about RV spot water hookups (we brought our own water). A great hiking trail across the parking lot - it’s not quite 2 miles, is flat and goes through forest and marsh areas in a big loop. That was an enjoyable find. This park is nothing special, but certainly better than spending even more hours sitting in traffic on a closed freeway! I’d stay here again. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/159948 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.452240" lon="-120.525230">
  <ele>1211.4</ele>
  <time>2024-05-17 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Husky Station</name>
  <desc>Husky station as you arrive in Princeton from the west. Fuel, bathroom, and air only. Previously had a water tap which is still signed, but is out of service, possibly due to the local boil water advisory resulting from the 2021 flood taking the pump station out of commission.  Air pump is around back.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-17 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/159953 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
