 <wpt lat="51.897269" lon="-68.166149">
  <ele>522.9244476817548</ele>
  <time>2024-06-02 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Riverside spots</name>
  <desc>Just to the north-side of the signs about the old mining town, look for a very short dirt-trail down to the riverside. There are several areas open and flat. Lovely views of the river and not much road noise. Its a bit rough to get down there, but most overlanding rigs and vans should make it without problem. Plenty of space for larger rigs, just walk it first to check that your vehicle could make it down okay (and back up in the morning!). No facilities. Free. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-02 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/160947 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
