 <wpt lat="44.819856" lon="-77.222036">
  <ele>99.2</ele>
  <time>2024-07-01 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Crownland</name>
  <desc>A wonderful crownland camp site near Bon Echo provincial park with lots of room for a couple tents. It has a little campfire area set up and a log seat, right on the edge of a lake. Also has a “take some leave some” pile of wood under a tarp, but make sure to try and leave some if you take!! &#xA;&#xA;How to find it: You’ll arrive at a dirt road with a sign that says “Skoot Damn” on it, and if you park up on the sides of that road to keep it clear, you’ll find the site by walking down the hill and turning right when you see a path in the forest. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-01 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/162613 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
