  <time>2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>White Butte Ski Trails</name>
  <desc>Parking lot for the ski trails. Looks like a place for people to walk dogs or hike in the summer. No signs banning overnight camping. Associated with local ski club, but it is public land. Some noise from street and trains but fairly quiet at night. Only a few other locals when we arrived at 9 pm. We stayed one night without issue.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/164092 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
