 <wpt lat="45.024221" lon="-65.095635">
  <ele>10.3</ele>
  <time>2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Sand Bank</name>
  <desc>There&#39;s a grassy clearing atop the bluff, overlooking the ocean.  There is an established fire pit  and room for maybe three tents comfortably. &#xA;The gravel road, that reaches to within 25m of the clearing, is accessible by car, if moving slowly. &#xA;Enough room to turn around at the road end,  or atop the hill,  120m back from the end. &#xA;Strongly recommend against trailer access,  but a really nice spot to tent on the bluff or truck camp at the road&#39;s end.&#xA;From the left side of the clearing,  there&#39;s a rope to help you back up the steep trail to access the rocky beach below.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/165495 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
