  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="44.867612" lon="-64.897790">
  <ele>8.7</ele>
  <time>2024-07-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Cloud Lake Boat Launch</name>
  <desc>It&#39;s a large, level gravel parking lot with a couple low key tent sites located in the woods around it.  &#xA;There&#39;s a rather small beach portion that blocked off with boulders (assuming for a safe place to lounge without a risk of getting run over), and a small water access to the left of that of which you can back your small boat trailer into the water.  It&#39;s normally quiet, with a random atv stopping in to check out the lake.  The Air Cadets do their camping phase here,  and occasional military camping/bbq functions are held here also.  Even though,  it&#39;s government maintained,  it&#39;s still Crown Land inside of the Cloud Lake Wilderness Area and is own to anyone that wishes to go there. &#xA;cell reception is spotty, at best,  and the strongest signal is in the middle of the gravel lot. There are no facilities on site.  &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/165879 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="45.530318" lon="-75.986818">
  <ele>70.32587316018493</ele>
  <time>2024-06-02 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Dead End Luskville Falls</name>
  <desc>Nice place for one night or two. Not a campground. But if you drive down to the dead end there is enough room for a campervan to park up for the night right next to the entrance to the trail to Luskville Falls. No amenities, bins or toilets so you need to be self contained. We had a 170 extended Sprinter, no space for big rigs though. No signs saying you cannot park there for the night. Quiet in the day and night. Not sure if its much busier in the Summer. Trail is a really nice hike! &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-02 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/165887 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
