  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2024-05-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Nanaimo River. Scout Hut Road</name>
  <desc>We found this beautiful spot at the Scout Hut Road. Shortly after the Spruston Staging Area you have to pass a gate (closed between 6p.m and 6a.m.). This road is not that bad, but for the Scout Hut Road we would recommend a 4WD. To get to the spots it’s not that far, but it took us some time. The sites are obviously build and used by locals. There is enough space for more then 20 cars, and there many different spots with firepits along the road. No toilets, so pack your shovel. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/174709 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
