  <name>Crystal Crescent Beach Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Possible to sleep in gravel parking lot. Park closes officially at 11pm, but gates were not closed. Police made a round around 9:30pm and did not bother us. Popular location in morning for dog walkers, very quiet during the night you can hear the waves. Beautiful fine sand and clear water. No signs regarding overnight parking. Pit toilets could be cleaner, and might be difficult to be level.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/174788 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
