  <name>San Juan River</name>
  <desc>If you follow the bad road from the bridge west all the way to a berm, turn left through some deep puddles and narrow sections you come out on the sandy beach of the San Juan River. Open, sunny, lots of room. Judging by the tracks it can be busy on certain weekends, but on a Monday night nobody was around. Definitely need high clearance and 4x4. Can&#39;t hear or see the road or anything. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-11-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/174817 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
