 <wpt lat="43.630009" lon="-80.475385">
  <ele>341.83316303215247</ele>
  <time>2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Township Road 60</name>
  <desc>Quiet spot right at an old bridge that has been closed for years. Used to be able to walk across now it’s all fenced off. Still a nice spot to park for one night or to hang out for the day. Lots of locals and fishermen frequent the area so be respectful. There is an unmarked trail to the side of the bridge but not sure if it’s private property or not. Limited turnaround room, vans and smaller rigs will be fine but I wouldn’t bring a trailer. Approx 2km of fairly decent gravel road to get here. I advise coming in from the East off of Katherine Street North - it is more level than the other side of the bridge. Remember bridge is closed so pick your approach! Couple small fire rings along the river. Keep it clean and respect the locals or it will get closed really quickly!&#xA; There&#39;s a snowplow turn-around for bigger rigs. Blink and you&#39;ll miss it. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/174991 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="53.712430" lon="-115.990430">
  <ele>779.6256103515625</ele>
  <time>2023-10-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>McLeod River Bridge</name>
  <desc>Right off of the highway, small road leading down to river on the East side of highway. Lots of space for big rigs, and smaller vehicles alike. You can drive along the edge of the river to a couple other spots, 4x4 not required but you&#39;ll want some clearance to access the left side. Rope swing under the bridge. Pretty neat spot. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/175067 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
