 <wpt lat="43.143016" lon="-79.045670">
  <ele>176.21103691495955</ele>
  <time>2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>River Road Pullouts</name>
  <desc>Just North of all the tourist craziness is a short road to the right if you’re heading north called river road right by the power plant. There are 6 picnic tables and pull outs along with three trash cans. On the other side of the road from the picnic areas is PowerPlant Property wetlands that are fenced off. For around 4 hours deer, turkeys, 3 foxes and other cool wildlife came to the fence line to feed. So if you sit in the area quietly it’s like a nature show. &#xA;&#xA;NEW: As already mentioned, parking is no longer permitted between 12 am and 6 am. We spent two nights on the asphalted lot opposite and nobody bothered us.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/175491 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
