 <wpt lat="49.542314" lon="-124.757490">
  <ele>2.0</ele>
  <time>2023-03-27 18:57:45 UTC</time>
  <name>Fillongley Provincial Campground</name>
  <desc>The Campground offers ten campsites located along the ocean, and there are several walking trails through the park where visitors can observe the old-growth cedar forest, a salmon spawning stream and remains of the old homestead.&#xA;&#xA;The Campground offers fresh water, pit toilets and fire pits at every campsite. All sites are open to online reservation.&#xA;https://bcparks.ca/explore/parkpgs/fillongley/&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-03-27 18:57:45 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/176243 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
