 <wpt lat="54.060410" lon="-119.011860">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2022-10-12 12:57:13 UTC</time>
  <name>Sheep Creek Prov. Rec. Area</name>
  <desc>Located directly on the river, separated only by trees. $20/night.&#xA;Sites 1 and 2 are &#34;first comes&#34; and self-registration. Sites 3-6 by reservation only via reserve.albertaparks.ca (two sites side by side each).&#xA;Four stars because as of early June 2022 and Saturday are all by themselves.&#xA;Small stone beach available. Otherwise there is not much to do here.&#xA;&#xA;Good to know: no hiking trails, 1 outhouse per gender, free wood, water via pump (non-potable), table bench and firepit per site. No net. No ATVs, snowmob. etc.&#xA;&#xA;(My review / view is compared to other places in BC/Alberta)&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-10-12 12:57:13 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/178662 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
