 <wpt lat="49.306925" lon="-115.081626">
  <ele>923.8396905401509</ele>
  <time>2023-08-28 10:24:08 UTC</time>
  <name>River Road</name>
  <desc>Drove a little past the first site shown for this area (2.2km away). Follow what I assume to be a logging road for about 10 minutes. The road is full of potholes so drive slowly! Eventually, you’ll see a spot on the right side of the road (could probably camp there).  If you’ve got a 4x4, you’ll see a small path to the left that’s fun to drive down. Follow it till the end (no space to do a u-turn. At the end you’ll be right by the water with campfires and a dump bucket (dig your own hole). Train tracks are 20 feet away and we had 3 trains come by at night. So be prepared for loud noise. I sleet like a rock so I was fine with it. There is one bar of cell service. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-28 10:24:08 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/179474 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
