 <wpt lat="53.323029" lon="-117.857762">
  <ele>1029.1280517578125</ele>
  <time>2023-07-19 21:18:10 UTC</time>
  <name>Brule Lake Campgroud</name>
  <desc>This is a small forest campground with large sites, free wood, and pit toilets. Wasn&#39;t to busy on a weekend and was relatively quiet. Several family groups out four wheeling and side by siding. Pay station $10 a night. Well worth it! Located off 40 between Hinton and Grande Cache. There were also several free areas off the road to Brule to boondock for free, however there were actually more people there then in this little campground. Active trains but no horns.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-19 21:18:10 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/179509 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
