 <wpt lat="51.083823" lon="-115.100813">
  <ele>1277.3115234375</ele>
  <time>2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Bow Valley Campground</name>
  <desc>Nice Provincial Park Campground with over 100 sites, some are riverfront. Many have electric and water. Several hiking trails and a camping store with lots of supplies including firewood. Hwy 1a is across the river and traffic can be noisy during the day but better at night. There&#39;s also a train track that parallels Hwy 1a and trains can be loud but I didn&#39;t hear any overnight. Sani-dump is located towards the exit. As for prices. I paid for an electric/water site and bought a bundle of firewood. The receipt was not itemized but I paid $57 CA&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/179984 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
