 <wpt lat="49.921682" lon="-117.383370">
  <ele>810.1656494140625</ele>
  <time>2024-07-06 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Bannock Point Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Driving down a gravel from the highway (no signs, not on google maps; ~2km past Bannock Point Campground when coming from Slocan), this will lead to a hidden parking lot in the forest (after the quarry) where you can sleep in your car. But walking down to the beach (1.2km) there is also an established free Recreation Site tent-campground next to the lake where you can swim and jump from small cliffs. Strongly recommended to go tenting, as the parking lot itself is boring. Pit toilets are both at the parking lot and the campground. No bear-catches. No trashcans, so PLEASE carry out everything to preserve this spot... I collected a whole bag of trash... Also please use the installed fire pits instead of making new ones.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-06 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/180381 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
