 <wpt lat="56.092322" lon="-130.045019">
  <ele>599.802734375</ele>
  <time>2024-05-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Glacier toe Overlook </name>
  <desc>Great overlook of the Salmon glacier toe and the river. We tried to get up to the proper overlook but the bulldozers had the road blocked and we’re clearing the snow. Impassable today and a few more days perhaps. We turned around and found this wide overlook. Not a bad place to make due. We are here early season with very few people on the road. Fallen logs on the road but passable yo this point. Campers, motor homes and cars all traveling this far. There is a garbage bin here, a small waterfall making noise beside us, a lovely view of the river below and the toe of Glacier. No cell service. We set up our Starlink for service. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/180560 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
