 <wpt lat="49.156085" lon="-123.170296">
  <ele>-11.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Richmond Street parking by laundromat</name>
  <desc>we parked with a 38ft fifth wheel to do laundry and decided to stay while we visited Vancouver. We parked for 2 nights, cycled to the Richmond metro, took the train to the city ($11 for the day) and had no problems. &#xA;Theres a water fountain opposite the laundry by the lights on the cycle path with a bottle filling nozzle &#xA;This spot is right on the cycle path, 5 mins from a big pump track. &#xA;Same as any street parking in Vancouver there is a couple or houses near by so I don&#39;t think it will last forever but use it while you can. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/181202 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
