 <wpt lat="48.031170" lon="-66.370791">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Eel River Bar Beach</name>
  <desc>Nice spot by the water, by the bridge and before the city park ,good cell signal. People making fire by the water. flat surface. sounds of the waves when high tide. locals come and collect shells and very friendly. you can walk when tide is low and swim water shoes would be recommended as it is rocky. there are signs of no camping but further towards the park. some restaurants nearby I was told by locals btw this is on Eel River Bar First Nation land.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Unknown&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/181572 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
