 <wpt lat="49.503210" lon="-55.646310">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Triton Sperm Whale Pavilion</name>
  <desc>Gravel parking lot next to the Sperm Whale interpretive pavilion, with a nice view of Butler’s Bight.&#xA;&#xA;We talked with Terry at the interpretive center - a super nice guy and a fountain of knowledge about sperm whales. Seriously. He also gave us his blessing to stay in the lot overnight and use the water spigot for potable water. No whale today but they had one here yesterday.&#xA;&#xA;Some road noise, but virtually vanished after sunset.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/181598 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
