 <wpt lat="43.154359" lon="-79.193940">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-11-11 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>St. Catharines Museum &amp; Welland Canals Centre</name>
  <desc>Large, mostly level, paved parking lot along a bike path and adjacent to a playground with killer views! When I asked if we could stay here, I never dreamed they&#39;d say yes. Their only request was that we park as far away from the building as possible but not in the lot belonging to the hockey ball club. It was easy to see where she meant. &#xA;&#xA;The museum has bathrooms, but only during business hours. There was a portapotta out front. Yes, the path and parking lot were busy in the evening, but it was a pleasant kind of busy. When we left at 7:30 am, there were 5 other vehicles in the large lot, all using the path. The ships might wake you during the night as the enter and exit the lock, but watching them go through the canal was awesome!!!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-11-11 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Unknown&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Unknown&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/181672 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
