  <ele>110.14872222673148</ele>
  <time>2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Crémaillère Harbour Overlook</name>
  <desc>Primitive site off of American Drive with a beautiful overlook of the Harbour. Recommended by a local working at the Viking Site L’anse aux Meadows. The road in here has some deep potholes and recommend a 4WD vehicle and a small trailer at most. Can be sketchy if you have any lightning at this higher altitude though. But the view of the Harbour with icebergs flowing through is phenomenal. There’s also 4 bars of 4g which definitely helps for mapping your next adventure!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/181992 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
