  <ele>18.130309867672622</ele>
  <time>2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Crémaillère Harbour </name>
  <desc>Southwest side of Crémaillère Harbour in between St Anthony and Goose Cove. Primitive camp site 50 meters from the Harbour. Beautiful site and no one else is here. Definitely need a 4WD vehicle to get down from the main road and can accommodate a small trailer. 4 bars of 4g down here which is remarkable. The ice berg mentioned yesterday from the hilltop north of Crémaillère Harbour hilltop split in two and flipped over. Pretty cool. Lots of black flies so bring the deet and they will leave you alone. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/182087 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
