 <wpt lat="53.925151" lon="-122.383539">
  <ele>748.5758056640625</ele>
  <time>2023-10-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Tabor Recreation Area</name>
  <desc>This is a trail head for winter activities, such as snow mobiles and cross country. The sign says that you can also hike the trail, but the weeds and wild flowers were a couple of feet high on the trail. It&#39;s a nice big parking area, plenty of room to turn a small rig around. There is a shelter here as well; it&#39;s a train car. This is not very far off the highway, but I felt comfortable  having the dogs off leash and on voice control. People driving by can not see into the lot. There is signage at the entrance. The mosquitos here were not as bad as a couple of other places I checked out. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/182436 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
