 <wpt lat="45.841009" lon="-60.147946">
  <ele>23.154623449780047</ele>
  <time>2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gabarus Lighthouse Open Space </name>
  <desc>A big open space by the ocean before getting to the light house (see pics). It doesn&#39;t look like the parking lot but I assume it is the parking for the lighthouse because you can&#39;t park at the lighthouse even though you can drive up. There&#39;s no parking next to the lighthouse, it&#39;s a dead-end road and quite narrow, at the end there&#39;s space to turn around, but if you park there and another vehicle comes up, they won&#39;t be able to turn around. Plus, this spot is more beautiful than the spot next to the lighthouse which is surrounded by bushes. The lighthouse is beautiful and very nice landscape, definitely worth a visit. It&#39;s super nice, quiet, and dark here. There&#39;s no facilities around, only a trash bin. Reception is very weak here, and I&#39;m using telus, but if you go farther south toward St Peter&#39;s on Fleur de lis trail, many places do not have reception at all, and some part is long gravel road. If you go that way, make sure to fill up the gas tank and your vehicle is in good shape since there&#39;s no service around and you can&#39;t even call emergency. It&#39;s therapeutic to not have reception occasionally though. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/182942 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
