  <ele>186.12148666381836</ele>
  <time>2023-08-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>W Darcy McKeough conservation area</name>
  <desc>This is a conservation area created when the flood control works were created. It is a large parking area with room for several vehicles. It is well shaded and very quiet. It appears that the locals use the area for ATV’ing. We heard them in the distance but didn’t see anyone. Very quiet and secluded spot for an overnight stay. No signs posted saying you can’t stay. As it’s a conservation area, no campfires allowed. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/183051 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
