 <wpt lat="47.620740" lon="-53.208210">
  <ele>3.0</ele>
  <time>2024-06-06 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Three Sisters / Mad Rock / Heritage Trail</name>
  <desc>Room for several small campers. One site has a picnic table. This area is maintained by the town and overnight camping is ok. There is a private property sign claiming ownership of the cliffs but this is disputed by the town and the locals. There are steps down to the rocks called Three Sisters. Many locals come by to run their dogs.&#xA;&#xA;To do:&#xA;There is a trail starting at the end of the road for hiking.&#xA;&#xA;There is the Mad Rock and ocean scenery -- whales are common in the summer.&#xA;&#xA;There are three large rocks called the three sisters. There is a set of metal steps leading down to the water.&#xA;&#xA;You can park and spend the night. There is also a picnic table.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-06 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/183234 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
