 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="56.018730" lon="-122.171062">
  <ele>657.9200039589214</ele>
  <time>2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Beach front camping</name>
  <desc>Awesome wild camping spot right next to Winston lake. It literally feels like camping next to the sea. Make sure to catch the  sunset. A local recomended this spot to us as a free/wild camping option in the area. Good cell phone service. &#xA;&#xA;Directions: As you drive up Canyon Dr to the dam you will pass Trapers Cabin Recreation Site, follow the road around the next corner and you will see a wide gravel road on your right leading down to the lake (satalite images will help to find it).&#xA;&#xA;Camping Spots: Now you have two options.&#xA;Option 1 : on the right side of the road is a huge area with plenty of spots to choose from (suitable for big rigs). If you choose this area, take the first or the second entrance (the third one you see on the satalite image is a steep ATV track). &#xA;&#xA;Option 2: if you follow the road further down it takes you directly to the lake, it is not too steep but a little bit rough... I made it in my 21ft 1976 Class C GMC with no problem. 4 wd not needed on dry days but definitly a bit of clearance and  some confidence (you want to avoid a few pointy rocks). &#xA;Once you’re down there is enough space to turn around and the sand is pretty firm and good to drive on (as water levels are changing here walk down first and check if there&#39;s actually enough space for you). Don&#39;t park to close to the cliffs if you don&#39;t want to get covered in dust as some sand chunks are breaking off.&#xA;&#xA;The Beach: Very fine sand/dust, lots of driftwood, very shallow water for the first 150m, beautiful sunset! &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/184488 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
