  <time>2022-10-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Morice Lake Camprground</name>
  <desc>Wonderful secluded Free Provincial Park campground - pit toilets - picnic tables - fire rings - very quiet - room for big rigs to tents - our Overland Rig enjoyed the journey here past the intersection where the First Nations group is protesting the pipeline - no issues  passing by - security was present at the intersection where the protest takes place - using the Starlink system to post this - no cell service here  - absolutely worth the effort to get here!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-10-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/184578 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
