 <wpt lat="44.925976" lon="-78.722834">
  <ele>259.3</ele>
  <time>2022-07-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Threaded water spout 25c/4L</name>
  <desc>A water spout poking out the back of a city-owned brown building. 25 cents (coins only) for 4 litres of water, dispensened from a spigot that appears to have threads for a hose, although I did not test to see if a hose would fit. Sign says it is treated and tested by the city once a week, and it most likely comes from the nearby river but I&#39;m not certain. Not sure if operable during winter months, but I would think it would be. We saw several people filling up jugs when we were there.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-07-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/185409 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Water</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>amenity_drinking_water</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
