 <wpt lat="46.234932" lon="-63.119095">
  <ele>0.2928469181060791</ele>
  <time>2024-07-08 09:22:38 UTC</time>
  <name>Municipal Carpark </name>
  <desc>Large carpark in front of the cruise ship pier and beside the PEI Urban Indigenous Centre which has its own small parking lot (do not park there). Go to the large, paved municipal lot next to it. Will be busy during the day but quiet after 9 pm. There is an aggregates site beside the water and if they are in operation, you may hear them in the early morning (not noisy but there can be operational noise of trucks and heavy machinery). No Frills store, good cell service on Bell. Short walk to downtown for bars/restaurants etc. Access to toilets during the day at the nearby food market.  Receiver Coffee - Brass Shop is good for early morning coffee (7 am), washrooms and breakfast (they bake their own bread). Good for a night right downtown near the harbor.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-08 09:22:38 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/186161 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
