 <wpt lat="52.683485" lon="-121.547322">
  <ele>999.4</ele>
  <time>2022-08-02 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Wolverine BC Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Small, quite remote recreation site next to a lake. There&#39;s a table, 2 fire pits and a user-maintained pit toilet (which was very clean when we came). There&#39;s room for a small RV, however the trail that leads to the site seems to get easily muddy and has several potholes, so be careful, especially on rainy days, and avoid this site if you have a really big rig. &#xA;The lake unfortunately makes a perfect nest for quite a few mosquitoes and does not seem swimmable, which is the only negative aspect of this site. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-02 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/186234 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
