 <wpt lat="51.181886" lon="-115.575656">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2022-08-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Train Station</name>
  <desc>On the right of the train station visitor information kiosk, there’s a tap on the wall. We asked the train station staff about filling our tank from there, and they said ok, but also informed us that the pipes are probably full of lead and they wouldn’t drink from it if they were us. Bottom line is only fill here if you have an adequate filter that filters out heavy metals. The blue in-line RV filters are usually good enough for that. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/186429 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Water</type>
  <extensions>
