 <wpt lat="49.441110" lon="-117.271310">
  <ele>3500.0</ele>
  <time>2022-09-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gold Creek Road Pullout</name>
  <desc>Cozy spot particularly suited to smaller overlanding vehicles, up to 22’ Class B RV (Sprinter Winnebago Revel in my case). There’s certainly the larger spot a bit further up road (see nearby iOverlander post), but unfortunately that one is fairly trashed (TP strewn about) and better for a larger group anyhow. Explore both and lock-in whichever suits your needs best.&#xA;Plenty of signs indicate burn restrictions and pre-established fire pits exist - no signs indicating ‘no camping’.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/187764 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
