 <wpt lat="49.443950" lon="-114.324529">
  <ele>1273.6048381880594</ele>
  <time>2022-08-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>castle falls provincial park</name>
  <desc>not the best provincial park we have stayed nor the cheapest but it&#39;s okay.  sites are on the small side, no views, but still room for big rigs if you get a spot. The falls are GREAT for a cold swim or a jump but not much else to around. &#xA;There is first come first serve spots on the road on the way in but as of aug 2022 this is not stated on their website or anywhere else since they are new this yr. &#xA;camp ground $26cad/night plus $12 booking fee if booked online&#xA;first come first serve $15/20 per night cash &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/187766 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
