 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.836041" lon="-119.481242">
  <ele>346.85458651557565</ele>
  <time>2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Okanagan Regional Llibrary</name>
  <desc>Large parking area in front of the library &amp; news center. No signs that overnight parking is prohibited. A bit noisy until 11pm as Gordon street is busy and it is also used as a bus terminal. The parking is large enough though so it is not too disturbing. Behind is the building is the Mission recreational park in which there are signs that it is open from 6 to 11pm and you ould be towed. During the day you can use the bathroom inside the building. You can also use the showers of H2O (open until 9 pm) if you buy a day ticket ($12). H2O also has guest wifi. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-17 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/187780 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
