 <wpt lat="60.217982" lon="-134.618369">
  <ele>755.0</ele>
  <time>2024-05-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Small pull off area near lake</name>
  <desc>Since the places before here had &#34;no camping&#34; signs posted, I kept going looking for a turn off. This is not that far down the road and still has beautiful views of lake and mountains. It is next to the road but quiets down at night. There are also a lot of cool plants around here so make sure you walk around and check it out while your here, if it&#39;s not too dark yet. Once we got settled inside our truck camper, we did hear howls and were not gonna come back out. The morning was perfect for a little walk before heading back up tagish rd headed toward Atlin. If you try you can get quite level in a small rig (van, truck camper). I would not recommend this for bigger rigs. We would stop here and stay again if necessary.  I have 3 bars of T-mobile service here as well and it&#39;s not far from Carcross.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/187855 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
