 <wpt lat="50.771828" lon="-68.655195">
  <ele>395.04840087890625</ele>
  <time>2023-06-22 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Deep pullout 20 km N. of Manic 5</name>
  <desc>This pullout is quite deep. It allows parking for the night at about 100 ft from the road. Seems sufficiently far for noise and dust from passing trucks and cars. The surface is sandy and somewhat level. &#xA;This was quite good for the night. This part of the unpaved between Manic5 and approx. Gagnon is nearly ready to be paved and looks very promising in terms of quality of road. The section from Gagnon to labrador border (&#34;mine service road&#34; near railroad with 10 to 15 railroad crossings is the section of the 389 that does not look like ready for prime time the next few years.&#xA;photo of deep pull out site. A few trucks around 10 pm and 7 am. Quiet in between. Certainly no locals!&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-22 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/188847 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
