 <wpt lat="45.092422" lon="-64.357162">
  <ele>7.913241704925895</ele>
  <time>2024-07-16 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Wolfville</name>
  <desc>Right in downtown Wolfville. The sign at the front says:&#xA;All Day Parking. Overnight Parking Permitted&#xA;Owner assumes all risk. Until further notice&#xA;&#xA;Two Sprinters and a small tear drop trailer spent the nigh,t no problem.  Lots of other cars parked overnight.  Very quiet against the Bay and there is a lovely walking path, dogs allowed on leash.&#xA;We all had our windows open, but lights were off and all campers remained low-key.  I didn’t see a bathroom anywhere, but we have our own.  Please remain self-contained and do not come here if you cannot fit within a regular parking spot.&#xA;&#xA;That means that if you use a generator, put out slides, set up chairs outside:  go to the nearby Walmart so you don’t ruin it for everyone else.&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-16 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/189214 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
