 <wpt lat="50.225840" lon="-126.646300">
  <ele>107.77727655112716</ele>
  <time>2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Nimpkish alternate</name>
  <desc>Lovely large clearing along the Nimpkish, at least when water levels are low. When driving the gravel road under the power lines, take the twin track dirt road to the left. Follow it along past a few forested spots until it ends at the river. I’m told there can be a muddy splash hole near where it comes out to the river. Had a couple of bars of LTE. &#xA;&#xA;Rocky /Gravel can be soft so easier to get stuck w/o 4 wheel drive but not so much if you stick to the spot up higher. &#xA;&#xA;If you’d rather not come to this spot on dirt road, just following the gravel under the power lines to where it ends is a great spot too already listed on iOverlander. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/189621 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
