 <wpt lat="59.535107" lon="-112.231641">
  <ele>278.1671389322728</ele>
  <time>2022-08-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Pine Lake Campground</name>
  <desc>Campground in Wood Buffalo National Park with approximately 20 unserviced sites (include 3 drive through sites for larger trailers). Pit toilets, free firewood, picnic tables, cooking shelter and sandy beach. Lovely forested sites.  Approximate 1 hour drive on gravel road (easy driving -  cars fine) from Fort Smith.  Hiking trail starts in campground.  $16.75/night. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/189744 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
