 <wpt lat="52.380866" lon="-126.458213">
  <ele>173.87469125059098</ele>
  <time>2022-08-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Blush Road</name>
  <desc>Not the nicest. Just a pull-out along the single-lane forestry road that leads to Mosquito Pass viewpoint. But big enough that we felt we could spend the night without obscuring traffic. Definitely wouldn’t take big rigs down it. We are pushing our luck with our 23ft ig. Road in has lots and lots of potholes. I guess if you take it slow in a bigger rig you’ll be okay. But definitely not ideal. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/189900 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
