 <wpt lat="50.445036" lon="-96.560620">
  <ele>196.37841796875</ele>
  <time>2023-06-14 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Public parking </name>
  <desc>We wanted to go to Beaconia Beach originally, but the road was flooded. A bit earlier on the beach access road we found this small gravel lot. Locals confirmed it&#39;s public land. There is a public drinking water source where cars come by to refill water tanks (so can you). The last car showed up before it got dark; first car again around 7 in the morning. Other than that very quiet. So only good for a night of sleep in a small vehicle, not really suited for a lot of cars to park due to the people coming and going for water.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-14 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190011 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
