 <wpt lat="50.232764" lon="-125.942888">
  <ele>170.9173193797469</ele>
  <time>2022-08-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>WR305- blocked road site</name>
  <desc>A small spur road that has many felled/fallen trees crossing it about 40 meters in, which makes it a nice little spot to spend the night as there can’t be any through traffic. There’s a nice little mossy carpeted forest around it, and even though it’s been logged and thus not easily traversable, the newer trees have grown tall and the place still has a magical quality to it. A nice little boondocking spot. No signal. Quiet, except of course when the occasional vehicle drives by. Room for several vehicles if you’re all traveling together. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190144 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
