 <wpt lat="48.483626" lon="-58.264437">
  <ele>8.290559734702088</ele>
  <time>2022-08-31 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Barachois Pond Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>The showers are super clean, park is very well maintained, and the view of the mountains is superb. Water was Luke warm to me, not hot, and you can&#39;t adjust temperature. Since hot water is on demand, it can be different each day. &#xA;&#xA;If you have NL park pass, you can go to any provincial park for shower, they also often have sanitary dump station with potable water to fill up. The year round park pass is only $50, where as day pass is $10.50, much better to purchase seasonal pass if you plan to travel across Newfoundland, since many provincial parks here are campground with shower facilities. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-31 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190161 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Showers</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_viewpoint</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>star</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#ffff80ff</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="50.136426" lon="-115.477023">
  <ele>1130.593593597412</ele>
  <time>2023-07-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Tiny spot by the lake</name>
  <desc>cute little spot on the side of the lake. Not really levelled but you can make it work. It’s worth the view and being 2ft from the lake. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - Not at Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190171 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
