 <wpt lat="52.358760" lon="-55.691850">
  <ele>10.0</ele>
  <time>2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Fishermen&#39;s Point</name>
  <desc>At the end of the village road, there is a picnic table, two benches and a small wooden gazebo. There&#39;s a park managed by St. Lewis Historical Society. Room for 1 vehicle (truck camper/van) overnight. Don&#39;t block turnaround or park in front of benches. Many locals come out to see fishermen&#39;s memorial or see the bay. Great view!&#xA;&#xA;A young lad who was the outdoor village caretaker told me I could put up my small tent. Initially I wanted to plant it at Deepwater Creek Trail, but he advised me not to, because of the bears roaming by the dump leading to it. So I spent a windy night by the sea, and watched the fishermen taking their boats out at sunrise.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190246 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
