 <wpt lat="52.689049" lon="-119.037809">
  <ele>756.4284616106107</ele>
  <time>2022-09-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Griffin Sawmill Rec Site</name>
  <desc>This is the smallest of the three official rec sites on the east side of the lake. About 10 sites total and mostly full this Labor Day weekend, but it is quiet as the other campers are respectful and the site layouts don’t work great for big groups. Access is a little more difficult, so no large RVs. Most sites have partial water view and shade from small aspen and cottonwoods. Rough boat launch most suitable for hand-carried boats. Clean pit toilet and garbage can. $14 a night collected by roving attendant.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190554 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.238164" lon="-53.485262">
  <ele>4.8</ele>
  <time>2024-07-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Alone at the beach</name>
  <desc>I know, there are a lot of places, but these could be one for 4x4 /6x6 offroad big rigs who are looking for loneliness. The sand is hard, so normally you shouldn’t have a problem. We entered it from the north. Beautiful spot direct on the beach. People just at weekends. We loved it. A lot of possibilities to walk. And beautiful for swimming.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190558 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
