  <ele>1424.388671875</ele>
  <time>2022-09-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Cows Meadow</name>
  <desc>A meadow with a very small creek normally used by a herd of cows, accessible only by 4WD, high clearance vehicles. For people who want/need privacy and are willing to go the extra mile to get away from the (Labor Day weekend) crowds. On public land: need to have a permit from https://www.alberta.ca/camping-on-public-land.aspx&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/190903 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
