 <wpt lat="49.085619" lon="-116.430370">
  <ele>707.5458984375</ele>
  <time>2024-05-06 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Canyon Park</name>
  <desc>Beautiful community space with 14 campsites (of which 4 in a loop for groups), sparkling clean showers (1$ coins) and flush toilets with hot water and sinks, even a fitness trail ! The quietest of the area, just 4 minutes away from highway 3. And only 20$ a night ! Self registration. First come first served. Only a couple of other campers last night, probably more busy during summer. We met the manager in the morning, very nice guy, and a bunch of volunteers cleaning up the facilities and getting ready for a community event. Really cool vibes here. With coyotes howling and owls singing during the night and the big open sky (just blurred by smokes right now sadly). Loved it, happy to add it to Ioverlander so others can enjoy it as well :)&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-06 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/191482 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
