 <wpt lat="49.841249" lon="-125.935318">
  <ele>240.7878098151047</ele>
  <time>2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Heber River Rec Site</name>
  <desc>If the Heber River rec site is full (only two spots) just go across the bridge and take the first right, down a gravel road for about 100m and then right at the fork, another 50m and there is one more spot with fire ring on other side of the river, with a small trail leading down to the water. No drop toilet on this side but you can fit a small camper down the road. It’s a little overgrown so if you’re worried about scratching up your rig you shouldn’t go down it. Bigger rigs might not be able to turn around. &#xA;&#xA;No cell service at all until near Gold River&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/192036 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
