 <wpt lat="60.679634" lon="-135.067759">
  <ele>734.0026072114706</ele>
  <time>2023-06-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Dead-end Road</name>
  <desc>Few hundred meters away from the Alaska Highway there is a dead-end road. The spots are directly on the „McLean Lake Quarry Rd“ which is blocked by big rocks, so there is no traffic anymore.&#xA;There is place for a RV directly in front of the rocks on the main road or another more leveled spot in a turn-out just 50m away.&#xA;&#xA;Great to stay there for a night and to be near to the city. Because nowadays it’s quite hard to find a free overnight space near to the city.&#xA;Nearly no noise from Highway! &#xA;&#xA;I have good 4G cellular network with TELLUS / BELL.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/192621 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
