   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="45.714245" lon="-63.291810">
  <ele>7.923785249702632</ele>
  <time>2023-06-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Patterson Wharf Park </name>
  <desc>The community park at the end of King Street which if a narrow un paved dirt Road leading down to the water.  it has picnic tables a deck overlooking the water also has a barbeque and fireplace built of stone. No signage, can park on the road.  No washrooms, water, or Wi-Fi, but a beautiful stop. I don’t see why you couldn’t set up a tent. &#xA;Restaurants up the road as well as other shops.  I parked under the bridge in front of a gate which serves to keep cars out, but there is an open access for pedestrians. The Bridge across the top, serves as a well maintained walking, hiking &amp; biking trail also part of the trans Canada trail.  &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/192624 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
