 <wpt lat="50.850319" lon="-110.696625">
  <ele>591.0</ele>
  <time>2022-09-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Buffalo Campground</name>
  <desc>A rural campground located in a beautiful wooded location on the North bank of the Red Deer River. At least 20 campsites but I didn&#39;t count them. All sites have picnic tables and fire rings. Toilets are outhouses. Entry fee is self-registration of $20.00/ night. There is a sign at the campsite that says work crew camping is not allowed. Excellent quiet campground in an out-of-the-way location. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/192837 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
