  <time>2022-09-22 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Turtle Mountain Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Campground was closed for the season so we spent a free night parked by the beach. Flush toilets were locked but there was a relatively  clean biffy. Loads of hiking trails in the park and maps available outside the campground office. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-22 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Unknown&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/192982 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
