 <wpt lat="51.897290" lon="-104.238231">
  <ele>502.15557861328125</ele>
  <time>2022-09-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Big Quill Lake</name>
  <desc>Big Quill Lakes is the largest north American salt water lake.  It is part of a bird migrating byway: sandhill cranes, snow geese, Canada geese, plovers, willets and much more.  The shoreline is muddy and rough so this is not a recreational lake.  The 17km of road off of the 16 from the south starts as gravel and becomes dirt (mud if wet).  The road is wide enough for a van to boondock but a big rig would cause a block.  The bridge to the north is washed out&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-09-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/193848 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
