 <wpt lat="50.439134" lon="-127.392812">
  <ele>51.9</ele>
  <time>2024-02-15 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Link river regional park</name>
  <desc>Beautiful campground on the lake. We drove through but didn’t stay but absolutely would. We are here on off season, mid September to end of May it is free first come first serve. Max 14 days. Pit toilets and fire pits. Multiple sites on the water. Also a river through the back. There was nobody there, I imagine on off season you could have it all to yourself. No cell service which is why we ended up across the lake but this is a great place!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-02-15 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/194743 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
