  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="45.243360" lon="-77.176360">
  <ele>249.8140720059497</ele>
  <time>2023-06-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>No Name Lake</name>
  <desc>Great site on a lake with no name, beside Cedar Lake. Go down through Lower Madawaska Provincial Park, following Hyland Creek Road until it forks into Hyland Creek Road and Two Island Lake Road, staying left on Hyland Creek road you’ll come up on a dirt road on the right side. Follow it until the end and there’s a site on the left on Cedar Lake and one on the right on No Name Lake. &#xA;&#xA;Someone was on the Cedar Lake site but it looked massive (they had 3 trucks plus ATVs etc.) and that’s where the sunset pictured is. &#xA;We stayed on the No Name Lake site and it was smaller and didn’t have the epic views but a great site none the less. All other Lake photos are no name lake- great for swimming and would be amazing if you had a canoe or kayak!&#xA;&#xA;No established fire pit or thunder box, so bring a shovel and prepare to be extra fire safe! &#xA;&#xA;Great area for 4x4 driving around lots of dirt road, missing etc.&#xA;&#xA;Defs need 4x4 to get here. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195114 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
