 <wpt lat="43.247668" lon="-81.824160">
  <ele>152.30855512612624</ele>
  <time>2023-08-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>The Pinery Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>This is a typical Ontario Parks campground.  Very nice, great beach, trails, this one even had a store.  Evening programs some nights, canoe rentals, etc.  This park has many hundreds of sites, some electric.  Expect to pay around $40C per night.&#xA;&#xA;My only complaint is that the showers were on the cool side (in mid-October),  however, most campgrounds are closed by this time of the year, so I am glad that I got a shower.  One of the other shower buildings had hotter water. Bathrooms and showers were exceptionally clean.  Sites all had plenty of privacy.  &#xA;&#xA;Overall a great park and campground.&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195356 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
