  <time>2024-05-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Port Elgin</name>
  <desc>Parking pull-out on a curve in the road at the north end of North Shore Park. This is not a formal site, but no signage prohibiting overnight parking. Right on the shore of Lake Huron with nice bathrooms and a splash park nearby. This site is also right beside a paved multi-use pathway that links Port Elgin to Southampton to the north. There is a fair amount of on-street parking in the town for overnighting. We stayed beside an elementary school located a couple of blocks south of Green St. There is free public wifi at the main beach parking lot, along with cold outdoor showers.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Cold&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195425 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
