 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="46.013470" lon="-60.399300">
  <ele>2.3164799258726423</ele>
  <time>2023-09-11 09:10:48 UTC</time>
  <name>Pullout off the causeway with picnic table!</name>
  <desc>There are 6 or 7 individual spots for vehicles to park! Each has a picnic table and it’s own little bay to hang out in. &#xA;The spots on either end of this causeway could accommodate larger RVs but the ones in between are smaller and best for vans or tents. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-11 09:10:48 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195438 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="43.804490" lon="-66.154181">
  <ele>4.053860958613267</ele>
  <time>2024-07-22 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>The road to Cape Forshu along False Harbour</name>
  <desc>There are several spots to pull out off the road next to the rock berm/ breakwater. You will be parked right next to the road but there is little to no traffic after dark. The end of this road is the famous lighthouse.  &#xA;There is access to beautiful False Harbour ( beautiful sand) and a short 3 minute walk away is yet another soft sand  beach! &#xA;We loved it so much we stayed 2 nights. Lots of locals walking dogs on the beach and all very friendly. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-22 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195441 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="44.045215" lon="-64.719224">
  <ele>3.654204897582531</ele>
  <time>2023-09-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Hank snow museum and free RV park</name>
  <desc>This is also listed as a formal campsite but I wanted to pin it again so people would know it’s free. &#xA;It’s a big open field bordering a pond with a walking trail. There are several picnic tables , garbage ( at the trailhead) and a gazebo. &#xA;Camping is free. Donations are accepted but I’m not sure where. &#xA;We stayed early October and we’re the only people here. &#xA;There is a dump station and water fill at the entrance on Hank Snow Road before you actually turn into the camping area &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - Not at Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195442 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="45.632505" lon="-61.959909">
  <ele>-59.46191741649386</ele>
  <time>2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Wildlife Management Area on Landing Rd</name>
  <desc>There’s a small parking area at the end of Landing road  with room for about 3 cars. Longer rigs could park beside the trees. &#xA;The road is quite potholed but if you go slow it’s manageable. &#xA;We didn’t spend any time at the river as it started to rain as soon as we arrived. We wanted an alternative to the Canadian Tire or Walmart parking lot and this fit the bill perfectly. It’s quiet and private and there’s lots of trees around. No “no overnight camping” signs. &#xA;There is a garbage can but no other facilities. There’s a hiking trail near the gate at the end of the road as well. Not sure how long it is or where it goes. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195445 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="45.675481" lon="-62.706493">
  <ele>6.351376715349332</ele>
  <time>2024-06-25 23:03:00 UTC</time>
  <name>The Old Pictou Railway Station</name>
  <desc>We liked this spot because it has a tall shelter that we could pull our van under to protect us from the rain while we cooked dinner on the bbq. It’s at the end of east Caladh Street overlooking the water. We checked out the laundromat as mentioned in another post. It’s the nicest one we have seen! Super clean with a bathroom and the option to just leave your laundry for them to do for you. Opens 8 am - 7 pm sharp. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-25 23:03:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195447 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="58.705355" lon="-124.896954">
  <ele>935.3261815682054</ele>
  <time>2022-07-31 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Camping beside the gravel pit with awesome mountain views</name>
  <desc>The access road to this spot is not marked on the highway but if you are travelling north towards Alaska then it’s the first left turn after you pass the sign for Wokpash Trail. If you miss that turn then you can also take the next left and it will get you on the same road. If you are southbound and you get to the Wokpash Trail turnoff then you have gone about 900 meters too far. We checked out both spots and preferred this one. &#xA;It was raining heavily when we arrived and the signs at Wokpash warned of flash floods. We already had an errant rock from a passing semi destroy our windshield today, we didn’t need any more drama. &#xA;The gravel pit is in between the entrance and exit roads and there are several nice spots to camp along the road or even closer to the gravel pit itself. The river was dry when we were there despite the recent rain so we just stayed near the gravel pit where drainage was good and the views of the surrounding mountains were quite spectacular. &#xA;We found lots of wild strawberries around as an added bonus. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-07-31 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195480 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="53.448378" lon="-122.559880">
  <ele>640.4401355236769</ele>
  <time>2023-06-20 08:03:38 UTC</time>
  <name>Hixon Falls - 4 km off highway 16</name>
  <desc>This is a great spot to spend the night but only suitable for smaller rigs like a van as the road in is a bit rough. &#xA;There’s room for 4-5 vans and we made it here in our Ford Transit no problem.&#xA;The falls are just a very short walk from the trailhead. &#xA;No cell signal and no trash cans so please pack out what you pack in. &#xA;If you don’t spend the night it’s also a great spot for lunch or a swim in the pools below the falls. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-20 08:03:38 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195486 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.807889" lon="-119.311745">
  <ele>1219.0</ele>
  <time>2023-04-29 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kelowna viewpoint</name>
  <desc>After the Myra Station Forest Road  campspot/fire ring, continue up the forest path (not the paved road, the forest trail which looks like an ATV track) for about 300m and you will come to this flat clearing with a large fire ring. amazing views of Kelowna, you can watch planes come in and out from the airport. 2 bars of service. totally secluded and quiet spot. Keep it clean and remember you&#39;re still in bear country! You will probably want 4x4 to get up the lane but super high clearance not required. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-04-29 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195554 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="45.591321" lon="-67.328272">
  <ele>134.39153809845448</ele>
  <time>2022-10-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>McAdam train station</name>
  <desc>Right next to train station so there is noise but only twice during the night so was ok. Road in front gets really quite after 6 pm 。gravel lot big enough to park 40foot rig with tow. No service. Telus has 4 bars so connection was good . &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-10-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/195580 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
