  <time>2024-06-16 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Teapot Mountain Trailhead</name>
  <desc>Little turnaround point/parking lot for the trail. Turn down Tallus Rd off hwy 97, stay right (on the road), watch for teapot mountain sign. Can park at the sign or continue up the narrow road. Made it up in my little 2WD, but I got out and walked up first because I wasn’t sure if I was going to make it. It’s gravel road from the hwy and has narrow one lane bridges. Nice clean pit toilet at trailhead. Beautiful hike especially at sunrise or sunset. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-16 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/201236 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
