 <wpt lat="44.293796" lon="-76.312407">
  <ele>78.46224594116211</ele>
  <time>2024-07-16 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Grass Creek Park</name>
  <desc>This is a beautiful large area that is maintained by the city of Kingston. There is a museum and as you follow down the road the next spot is a parking lot for the boat launch with an outhouse. If you follow the dirt road to the end, past the large dog park on the left-hand side you will come to the large parking lot for the playground and beach area. There is a washroom building. We stayed overnight with no issues. Lots of people around in the morning for the boat launch &amp; dog park. Beautiful spot on the water.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-16 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/218264 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
