 <wpt lat="53.181632" lon="-122.637086">
  <ele>781.5789794921875</ele>
  <time>2023-04-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>the moose spot</name>
  <desc>we found this spot at the end of April, looking for another pin as it was getting dark. it very muddy and a sign warning of a washout. we were looking for a place to turn around that wasn&#39;t too muddy or covered in snow. this gravel pull off worked perfectly, although there are tons of better spots along this route in the summertime. we saw a mother moose and her Calf trotting down the road. we continued as 30 seconds later saw 4 elk. the area is heavily logged. unsure if active logging is still taking place.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-04-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/218578 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
