 <wpt lat="49.013873" lon="-94.412848">
  <ele>293.69379114737666</ele>
  <time>2023-06-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Oscar&#39;s Bay Beach</name>
  <desc>Small public beach and picnic area with pit toilets. The water is high so most of the beach is under water, but it means swimming is great. Lots of shade and grass. Two large picnic shelters. The beach side of the park is gated and says no camping. The parking lot outside the gate holds 30 vehicles. Plenty of room to turn around. There is no signage indicating overnight parking is not allowed. This is clearly where the locals go to swim. Watch the lakes for the American White Pelican which nests here.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/218744 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
