 <wpt lat="43.049673" lon="-79.120535">
  <ele>143.9404296875</ele>
  <time>2022-08-07 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Jellystone Park </name>
  <desc>a family oriented campground suitable for all sizes of RV overlander or road only vehicles.  pets are allowed and it has a general store for most of your needs. close to niagara falls and safari niagara. good enough atmosphere staff were all friendly  ... has a pool bouncy pillow larger attractions as well (some require extra payment) but for our four kids there was plenty for them to do and keep them occupied when we were not sight seeing ;) they also have cabins, yurts, and trailers for rent as well if that is more your style. some of the sites are tight but cheaper than a hotel and better fires.. the wood sold here colst 11.30 CAD and was just under a cubic foot of good hardwood. close to a major highway but it is a place for the kids to burn off some energy and you get some rest.  would come back..&#xA;&#xA;we have had a minivan with a 1959 sportscraft 15 foot overall trailer. we were the tiny one of the bunch by far.&#xA;&#xA;happy camping &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2022-08-07 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - Not at Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: Unknown&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/219580 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
