 <wpt lat="58.104477" lon="-122.719826">
  <ele>568.1214599609375</ele>
  <time>2024-06-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Adsett Creek</name>
  <desc>Quiet spot on a bend of the creek right at the old decommissioned Alaska Highway bridge. Small, but super easy access, at this water level the creek is really mellow with a little beach to hang out on. Watched a family of 5 beavers on the ponds around until the mozzies got to me. Almost no cell service. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/220859 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
