 <wpt lat="46.442301" lon="-80.992033">
  <ele>283.8162408359349</ele>
  <time>2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Woods in the city</name>
  <desc>On the Algonquin road, there is a path at the end of the Remington road. It’s a long path, but there is an entry for a shorter path where you can park. Space for a car or two. For one night it’s pretty a good place because you are right in the city. &#xA;&#xA;We did sleep here for two nights, waiting to receive a part from the dealer. Pretty spot, we did a fire! &#xA;&#xA;No one bothered us, no lights, no facilities, but a lot of privacy here!  &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/220860 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
