  <ele>937.6866780212149</ele>
  <time>2024-07-15 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Porcupine Creek</name>
  <desc>Turn off on the north side of Porcupine Creek bridge. The dirt road leads to a wide open area about .5miles off the Alaska Highway. Clearly people have camped here as evidenced by the numerous rock fire rings. &#xA;No amenities at all. Pack it in, pack it out. No cell service. Ok for a night. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-15 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/222861 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
