 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="42.673561" lon="-81.108722">
  <ele>228.59999268480024</ele>
  <time>2023-10-18 11:51:05 UTC</time>
  <name>Solitude Nature Reserve</name>
  <desc>Amazing free campsite! Beautiful nature preserve with walking trails open to the public. Also 6 campsites (2 drive up, 4 walk-in tent sites) that are accessed thru a locked gate.  Contact the park, at https://solitudenaturereserve.com/location/  to reserve your site and get the code for the lock. The sign at the park says it is available for weekend camping but we contacted and asked to camp on a Sun and Mon night and that was ok. Our site was huge, plenty big enough for our 2 vans (we were traveling with another couple). There were 2 picnic tables, a fire pit, and a composting toilet at our site. Beautiful.flowers all around, nice morning walk on the trails. No payable water.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-18 11:51:05 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/223817 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
