 <wpt lat="47.808510" lon="-52.786640">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Cape St Francis Lighthouse.</name>
  <desc>Accessed from a lengthy gravel pot holed road.  Due to the lack of space to turn around when you reach the end you should only attempt this with a passenger vehicle, class B, small class C or a truck camper.  That said the views are spectacular.  There is sign where the road turns to gravel posted by the Canadian Govt advising 4x4 vehicles .   I could see this being a necessity in very poor weather. There are a few steep inclines. Should be a great spot to whale watch on a clear day.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Unknown&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/224391 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
