 <wpt lat="51.217660" lon="-116.638770">
  <ele>1058.3607032650623</ele>
  <time>2023-07-27 08:56:20 UTC</time>
  <name>Beaverfoot road</name>
  <desc>Nice spot just before km 3 on the logging road. Past the atv tours. &#xA;Nice wide road easy for large units. Not on the river but if your brave enough to walk over its not far. Great place with tonnes of room to play with dogs. Not a lot of traffic. Wapta falls is a couple km down the road but the drive in is NOT suitable for large rig. Very narrow and when it rains very sketchy. Park and walk in!  I did see a bear coming my way but a car scared it off :( Be aware of surroundings. It&#39;s a paradise here. Lots of nice free places along the road. If you have a smaller rig or 4x4 could explore other roads off the main. &#xA;Cell service is fine and my starling provided perfect internet.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-27 08:56:20 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/226018 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
