 <wpt lat="50.166209" lon="-126.304583">
  <ele>304.52567025517857</ele>
  <time>2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Shoen Lake Rec Site </name>
  <desc>absolutely stunning campsite, 6-7 flat sites with picnic tables, some amongst the forest and a couple right on Shoen Lake. well maintained with clean pit toilets. $11 a night per party (but a ranger came by and said as it&#39;s shoulder season not to worry). the lake is clear with crazy ghostly logs looming from the bottom, we had our kayak and thoroughly enjoyed going to the other end of the lake to explore the most beautiful swim spots. great fishing. if you get the spot to the right of the boat ramp you&#39;re in for the view of a lifetime with Mt Shoen towering over the lake, all framed by beautiful trees. stunning&#xA;the road in is super bumpy but doable in any car,just take it slow. no reception. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/226649 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
