 <wpt lat="49.099310" lon="-121.479000">
  <ele></ele>
  <time>2023-06-25 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Closed off logging road</name>
  <desc>Just down from the Chilliwack campground (two minute drive). There is a great spot for a campervan or tent. It looks like it must have been an old access point for logging trucks. It was a relatively quiet road - even on a summer weekend. There are some beautiful trails close by but we only had one family walk past our camper in two days. Pretty private! No signs saying no camping, there is an old fire circle. No reception. We ended up staying here two days instead of one because we enjoyed it so much.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/226700 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
