 <wpt lat="47.834819" lon="-59.337786">
  <ele>6.471102192997932</ele>
  <time>2024-05-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Codroy Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>No site markers. just a decent gravel parking lot just off 407 past the bridge, which has another free spot. Garbage bins and pit toilets. Beautiful view of mountains and also across the road are sand dunes to a nice beach area. Large enough lot for about 8 to 10 campers, vans. You could tent on the grassed area. some road noise until midnight.&#xA;&#xA;Being from Ontario, I say this is our version of a conservation area.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/226795 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
