  <desc>Small parking area at the trailhead, room for one 30&#39; or smaller. Right next to main road but not busy at all.  Several locals stopped by to chat.  Local seafood processor nearby, we picked up fresh Snow Crabs.  Glass Hole trail was a great hike.  Also site is where a 1942 Royal Canadian plane crashed.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-23 08:16:02 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/227031 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
