 <wpt lat="49.572591" lon="-121.911989">
  <ele>95.59945956510226</ele>
  <time>2023-06-29 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Random off road along Harrison Lake</name>
  <desc>Beautiful spot once you get here. The road down has limited turn around spots and is narrow. Once you go down this you are committed.&#xA;&#xA;You will need 4x4, high clearance, and SKILL to get to this spot. Once you get to a mini wash out you have to decide to go right or left. Both decisions are good and will reward you with views of the lake, mountains, a fire ring, and ample room to turn around. They are at the end of the road. Going left is the best decision in my opinion. &#xA;&#xA;This spot has the potential of eventually not existing because of the small wash out and no maintenance. &#xA;&#xA;Not good for big rigs and expect to get some scratches on your car on the way in and out.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-29 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/227365 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
