 <wpt lat="45.099381" lon="-67.054776">
  <ele>3.2062339782714844</ele>
  <time>2024-07-07 10:12:59 UTC</time>
  <name>Bar St entrance to Minister Island</name>
  <desc>This is a gravel lot that opens up to a road to Minister Island at low tide.  No toilet, no water but what a spot to watch the tides change.  We spent one night a few cars wandered down this way but no one bothered us.  There are no ‘no camping or overnight parking’ signs.  There is a garbage can.  &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-07 10:12:59 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/227666 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
