 <wpt lat="45.431862" lon="-73.665906">
  <ele>25.271153674460948</ele>
  <time>2023-07-02 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Park</name>
  <desc>I found this river view spot via iOverlander last night, but when I went to check in this morning, it was not showing up on the list no matter how I changed the settings.&#xA;&#xA;This is a small public parking area with room for about 10 cars to pull nose in. When I got here at midnight, there was one other car here. When I woke up at 5 am nearly all the spots are full of local cars. A few parked to go fishing on the pier and others were biking or jogging.&#xA;&#xA;There is a road behind the parking spots that had a fairly steady stream of traffic throughout the night. It was otherwise quiet. I felt safe.&#xA;&#xA;The best part was that I was able to walk along the river to a nearby Arboretum.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-02 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/227700 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="53.772527" lon="-112.775598">
  <ele>647.1686668395996</ele>
  <time>2024-06-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Public Park</name>
  <desc>This is a huge grassy, mostly level  field with picnic tables on one side, and, I believe, a Native American midden in the center. There are no ‘no camping’ signs, and we were sent here by a local at the gas station. There is room for multiple units. While it is on the corner of 2 rural highways, the noise level at bedtime was very minimal. Verizon coverage was good. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/227725 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="50.113044" lon="-120.787003">
  <ele>583.623779296875</ele>
  <time>2023-07-02 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Parking lot at Merritt</name>
  <desc>Parking lot in Merritt&#39;s Downtown. No sign saying &#34;no overnight camping&#34; and no limited time neither. We stayed 2 nights. Police patrol this parking, they said nothing to us. Was quiet at night, not busy during the day. Very nice brewery close by : Empty Keg Brew House, I recommend!&#xA;You can get visitor center&#39;s wifi but it&#39;s slow internet. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-02 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/227769 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.238810" lon="-121.767061">
  <ele>400.0</ele>
  <time>2023-06-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>OK Tire Agassiz</name>
  <desc>We needed to change 2 tires, they were ready to explode. This garage was on our way. Guys were super nice, they worked fast and explained us few things. 30 minutes after and we were on the road again.&#xA;We were lucky because they had 2 RV tires in stock but be aware that they might not always have RV tires. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-06-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/227770 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Mechanic and Parts</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>shop_car_repair</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#9999ff</osmand:color>
