 <wpt lat="53.532528" lon="-117.956262">
  <ele>1317.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Small forested clearing</name>
  <desc>Small clearing at the end of a cut line. Narrow trail on the way in, and just big enough for a vehicle, tent and campfire. &#xA;&#xA;Turn left off Rock Lake Road at the T-intersection, and then turn right behind the trees. Follow the grassy path, until it opens up into another small clearing. Straight ahead a cut line gives a view of the valley below. To the left is the narrow trail to a dead end, which made for a good private spot. Satellite imagery makes it pretty clear for navigation.&#xA;&#xA;There is a ridge to the north and east, so there can be some wind that passes through. We were battered with rain throughout, but despite, the spot was nice and quiet. Occasionally can make out a train in the distance, and really loud engines, but overall, pretty serene.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/228018 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
