 <wpt lat="49.656240" lon="-117.147380">
  <ele></ele>
  <time>2023-07-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>FSR Off of Kokanee Glacier Park Road</name>
  <desc>Follow Kokanee Glacier Park Road past the Kootenay Mountain Zipline. There will be 1 campsite on your left on the way up, go past it and take the first left on a FSR. You could make it with 2WD, but 4x4 would be better with the water run offs (your car may bottom out). We pulled up right beside the bridge, there was already a campfire set up. Stayed there for 2 nights and didn&#39;t see a soul! Went down to the provincial day use park beach to use the beach during the day, which is free AND has showers! Also super close access to mountain bike trails.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/228170 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
