 <wpt lat="44.281921" lon="-77.527195">
  <ele>161.8668336905339</ele>
  <time>2023-07-05 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Natural Spring (no hose)</name>
  <desc>There is a “parking” sign with no restrictions for overnight, however, the parking lot is rather small, and locals frequent… &#xA;&#xA;There is a sign stating that the water is not for human consumption, but I met 2 different locals there and asked them:&#xA;&#xA;Local #1 “We drink it all the time. You will be happy with this water. The city just doesn’t want to be liable if something happens, but they actually test it…”&#xA;&#xA;Local #2 “We only use it for cooking, but many people drink it and no one gets sick that I know.”&#xA;&#xA;I also met 2 ladies travelling from NY looking for clean water for their aquarium. I watched them test the water. In short, no junk and alkaline. That last part was a bonus&#xA;&#xA;It was a great little spot to get a splash of water and refresh from the heat. The bench and the way the water comes out made it great for a morning refresh!&#xA;&#xA;If you come from the south, follow the damn and you will see some parking spots, as well as a free splash park for young kids.&#xA;&#xA;I left a water dish for dogs here, in memory of my Little Bear who passed away recently.&#xA;&#xA;Although there are no restrictions, other than dumping, be kind. Respect this beautiful spot.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-05 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/228187 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Water</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>amenity_drinking_water</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#0099ff</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
