 <wpt lat="50.783955" lon="-120.895961">
  <ele>786.0747570702806</ele>
  <time>2023-07-07 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Sabiton Creek Rd</name>
  <desc>The turn off ofr highway 1 is tricky if you’re heading east as it’s right around a curve and two lane. The road is very rough with washboard and there are other sites on the way up but most are pretty exposed. This site is about 5 miles up off the blacktop and about 100 yards off of the dirt road. Tucked back in some pines between two small hills, it’s well sheltered from the wind and yet nicely sunny. No services at all. Pack it in, pack it out. 2bars ATT&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-07 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/228664 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
