 <wpt lat="50.676150" lon="-120.313240">
  <ele>330.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-13 03:08:37 UTC</time>
  <name>River Street - Gravel Lot</name>
  <desc>This is my second night here. I was going to stay at Pioneer Park, but since it has a gate, it has the potential to be locked (even if they are not doing it right now), so I came back here. There are 2 other rigs here now (1030pm). I like the river walk and the availability for somewhere safe for my dog to play. It is not as close to the train tracks either, which is nice. The sunsets here are beautiful, too. I saw the restrooms nearby, but I did not use them. There are ball games and people playing tennis across the street, which I dont mind at all. Feel perfectly safe. If I come back through here again, this will be my go-to campspot!&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-13 03:08:37 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/228731 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
