 <wpt lat="45.829743" lon="-77.106139">
  <ele>73.88006591796875</ele>
  <time>2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Ottawa River Walk-In Camp</name>
  <desc>This specific plot of land is largely ignored by the city. It&#39;s by far the most scenic view of the Ottawa River from central Pembroke. Its sheltered and private from the main Millennium Trail behind the Beer Store. No anti-camping signage, and the homeless of town haven&#39;t had issues occupying the various tent-camping spots available. Within walking distance of many amenities in town. River is shallow for quite a distance, but is still considered swimable! Accessible stairs from Algonquin Trail down to waterfront or Beach just a few more steps down trail...&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/228769 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
