 <wpt lat="50.220314" lon="-126.620206">
  <ele>110.62188720703125</ele>
  <time>2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gold Creek Bridge</name>
  <desc>North side of bridge has large areas on both sides of BC19 to pull off and spend the night. The west side of the hwy. has a path thar leads down to the creek. the site is on Rte 19 right beside the hwy so there is lots of traffic and noise early in the evening. if you face the river you will forget the hwy is behind you. we are in a 28 ft. class C and had plenty of room to turn around. Not sure you could do the same with a Tt.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/229133 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
