 <wpt lat="49.027890" lon="-118.679520">
  <ele></ele>
  <time>2023-07-01 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>McCarron Creek Road too</name>
  <desc>Turned onto McCarron Creek Road to see the camp site already listed.  Maybe OK for a camper van that doesn&#39;t mind being so exposed.  I drove further up the road as kiragillingwater&#39;s description suggests.&#xA;&#xA;At 4.3 km (2.7 m) I turned right onto a small seldom used forest access road.  A couple hundred meter and I found a nice grassy area that was very private.  The ground is a bit lumpy so you will have to move around a bit to level your rig.  Not too bad.&#xA;&#xA;Very quiet with only the sound of a small creek to keep you company.  During the evening and morning there were a few cars on the main road.  But, this site is out of their site.  There is also a farmhouse nearby but well out of site.  The tracks on this small side road indicate it might have someone come by every week or two.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-01 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/229148 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
