 <wpt lat="49.148421" lon="-97.170636">
  <ele>220.48992919921875</ele>
  <time>2023-07-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Old Dominion Dam</name>
  <desc>A small gravel loop with about 5 fire rings located next to the old Dominion City Dam.&#xA;A favorite spot to toss a line in and fish.&#xA;I stayed one night and had a couple roll through on their golfcart while I was setting up. They stopped to look at the dam, and moved on.&#xA;1030pm a muscle car started to pull in, then backed up and left when they saw my car in the shadows.&#xA;The grass is cut, there are small fire rings. No amenities on site, no garbage either.&#xA;I fluctuated between 1 bar of LTE and 3 H+ of service on Bell.&#xA;You can faintly hear the highway in the distance, but overall it was very quiet.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/229409 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
