 <wpt lat="54.824272" lon="-123.344912">
  <ele>855.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-11 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Carp Lake Campground</name>
  <desc>This is one of 5 campgrounds in this park (2 main and 3 island). The other main one is at War Lake (at the beginning of the park). Even though the road shows it keeps going after this campground,  it does not. This is the end. Joe (the host) was very nice and came to pick up the 20 CAN in the evening. The campground has a lot of spots, not all overlooking the river. If you want one of those, you might want to reserve it. However,  when we got here, there was only 1 other camper, now there are 4. I did not reserve and got a great spot. There are pit toilets scattered throughout and even a playground and horseshoes. There is also a boat ramp and place to clean fish. Walking around, we noticed a lot of stairs going down to the lake throughout the campground as well. I do not have dump tanks but checked on that, too, and it says it cost 5 CAN to use the dump station. There is no cell service. This was a beautiful and peaceful stay. Added photos. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-11 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/229792 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
