 <wpt lat="55.695832" lon="-121.638657">
  <ele>646.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>RV parking behind Visitor Center</name>
  <desc>This is the second year I have stayed here. Neither time had any issues. There are only 3 spots, long enough for a car and small trailer or even class c. I have a truck with a camper. There are no amenities, but that is ok for me. This is also by the fire department, and they have an ambulance here, so if there was an emergency, it might get loud. It is also on a slight slant, but I dont mind that either. I like the spot also because I am already here in the morning to go to the visitor center, no dropping my top just to drive here from another spot. Added photo. Would recommend. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/229947 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
