  <name>Champion Lakes Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Very nice provincial park. 90+ sites all clean, reasonably level, with picnic tables and fire rings. Pit toilets, flush toilets, potable water and trash. Probably one of the cleanest provincial parks we have been in. The sites are somewhat close together, so privacy is at a premium. There are huckleberries everywhere this time of year!  &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-11 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/230098 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
