 <wpt lat="49.511449" lon="-56.108323">
  <ele>24.42220169864595</ele>
  <time>2023-08-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Rattling Brook - Newfoundland </name>
  <desc>Just across the road from Rattling Falls Trail parking area. Beautiful clearing by fresh water Brook on one side - ocean view on the other.  There is a cookhouse gazebo. Platforms for renters and picnic tables.  Maintained by local volunteers. There is a book in the cookhouse to sign and some leave $5 or$10 donation in box. They provide firewood and garbage bags&#xA;For garbage containers and recycling.  Picturesque spot!  Enter just before you cross the bridge over the falls.  Sharpe right turn - down steep hill but easily maneuverable.   Enjoy -&#xA;We did!&#xA;I was able to get into area with my 32 ft Coachmen Leprechaun motorhome. Stay to the left and roll out onto the grass before turning to parking spot. My clearance is very minimal. My safety bar on my rear bumper rubbed a bit on the right side but not enough to damage anything. Just go slow. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/231344 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.634796" lon="-54.770958">
  <ele>12.155208078213036</ele>
  <time>2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Ragged Point</name>
  <desc>At the end of the road it gets a little steep and a bit rugged, then opens up. The last house on the road (Jeff) said it was ok out here - better across road from him, but steep and narrow - we chose the top&#xA;It got rough, but doable in 4wd Sprinter - would not take a big rig or low clearance van - several could camp - keep it clean and friendly!&#xA;&#xA;Jeff gave us iceberg bits and we visited home and neighbors/friends - we love these people and expect iOverlanders to respect the place. &#xA;Some locals had dumped trashy bits, perhaps to have a bonfire - go past that and it is rugged beauty&#xA;Several could park here and even spread out - but few would take the rough parts (but not horrible, just a challenge)&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/231362 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="62.576379" lon="-136.793583">
  <ele>784.7669468388666</ele>
  <time>2023-07-16 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Antenna campsite</name>
  <desc>A campsite for the adventurous. You’ll see the antenna on the hill while driving along the highway. No problems for motorbikes, although 4wds will get here, you’ll get a few scrapes. Gorgeous views of the mighty Yukon up nice and high. A decent map app will show you the track to get here. Could get very windy. Don’t bother with your big rig.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-16 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/231372 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
