  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="47.212835" lon="-52.845068">
  <ele>18.1</ele>
  <time>2024-06-28 09:14:56 UTC</time>
  <name>Tors Cove</name>
  <desc>Disused government dock, but used by locals and a few tourists  to enjoy the scenery.  Wonderful views of Fox, Ship and PeePee Islands.  If you have anything that floats, you can put it in and explore.  Peepee is surrounded by puffins floating in the water and has a colony you can see.  The other islands have literally thousands of gulls.  You can see sea caves, and a local farmer puts his sheep out on Ship and Fox Islands.  We even had dolphins swimming around us and a curious seal near the camping spot. &#xA;&#xA;Superb place - nothing fancy, no facilities, of course.  Although there are two overlanding spots, it really would be better to not camp at the one at the left of the boat ramp as people do come and go.  We camped on the right-hand side at an angle for complete privacy without feeling like we hogged the whole spot.&#xA;&#xA;Ok cell service too.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-28 09:14:56 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/232036 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
