 <wpt lat="54.294430" lon="-129.398050">
  <ele>14.813279525975055</ele>
  <time>2023-07-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kasiks/Skeena River Boat Launch </name>
  <desc>This spot is accessible at the GPS coordinates noted. The entry point is on the north side of the highway. If you’re coming from Terrace, you turn right, if you’re coming from Prince Rupert, you turn left. You will go past the initial parking lot, drive under the bridge, and drive to the end. There is a fire pit, and it is very tucked away. Traffic dies down at night and the train passed only once overnight. We could hear it very faintly because we were tucked in and far away from the train bridge. We had two bars of Telus (AT&amp;T) cell service. Only one vehicle (Ford Transit High Roof, Extended) or several tents can fit in to the little hideaway at the end. Take care of this spot and pack out what you pack in. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/232234 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
