 <wpt lat="44.619330" lon="-80.947510">
  <ele>154.7</ele>
  <time>2023-07-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Indian Falls Conservation Area</name>
  <desc>Parking lot in front of the Indian Falls trail. It is a paved, pretty level parking lot with running water toilets. No &#34;no overnight&#34; signs anywhere, but we stayed stealthy because there is a house near-ish. We were the only people parked there. Nobody bothered us and the first other people arrived at 7ish in the morning. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/232530 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
