 <wpt lat="63.229034" lon="-123.471756">
  <ele>127.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Sign on tree says : Camp spot #3</name>
  <desc>I came here on a Saturday evening and am stuck here due to the gas &#34;station&#34; closing at 4 pm on Sat and not being open on sunday. No one on my way up let me know that there are days it&#39;s not open. I will make sure to add a pin for that as well for others thinking about coming up here. I asked at the hall (middle of this village) where I could stay, and the closest was this spot. It is a field with some trees and a 2 track going diagonal through it. My Tacoma and truck camper made it just a bit bumpy. Honestly, I probably could have stayed anywhere, and it wouldn&#39;t have mattered. They also let me know the &#34;store&#34; is not open until 2 pm on Monday. I did not see a store going through, so I am not sure where it is. It is summer, so the bugs are bad, dogs walking free everywhere and almost endless light. It is super humid here and almost 90° F. So you dont want to cover up but have to due to the bugs. The river is beautiful,  but knowing what I know now, I wouldn&#39;t have made the treck up just to &#34;check it out,&#34; especially on a Saturday. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/232738 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="47.058303" lon="-52.910363">
  <ele>8.53690884821117</ele>
  <time>2023-09-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Calvert Harbour Beach</name>
  <desc>This site is about 5 min north of Ferryland. If traveling north on Route 10 the turn off is right onto North Side Road. It leads to the small community of Calvert. As soon as you pass the white building at the harbor dock, that once housed a fish plant, there will be a small gravel parking area. Picnic tables and benches were there.  Parked two class B vans for the night. We were invited to camp here by a local man who had boondocked for 40 years. Quiet night except for the soothing sound of waves. Very foggy so can only imagine the view. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/232757 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="46.648210" lon="-53.108842">
  <ele>40.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-22 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gravel pit above Criple Cove</name>
  <desc>Was going to stay at the lighthouse,  but foghorn was too loud for me, so had seen this one while heading in &#xA;At least a couple fairly level spots,  and a couple more not so level.   Easy maneuvering with a 19&#34; trailer. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-22 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/232767 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
