 <wpt lat="63.207338" lon="-123.411607">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-07-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Wrigley&#39;s &#34;Campground&#34;</name>
  <desc>There is a sign that says this is a campground and has 13 sites. It also said it has water, toilet, and garbage cans. It has none of those. All of the &#34;spots&#34; are marked on a tree, but thats the only way I knew they were spots.  Most have trees fallen or shrubs/trees growing in them. This campground is not useable. I am not sure how long it&#39;s been like this, but it looks like a long time. There is no place to actually camp around here, but I dont think they will have an issue if you ask and park near the main building where it is nice and graveled. Check the weather too before you go up. You dont want to get stuck in a thunderstorm you didn&#39;t know would happen because you went by Fort Simpson&#39;s weather. They are not the same.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/233086 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
