 <wpt lat="46.315256" lon="-81.649000">
  <ele>166.46000960562378</ele>
  <time>2024-04-29 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Riverside power line camp site</name>
  <desc>The nearby riverside wilderness camp site was occupied when I arrived around 7pm, so decided to drive a bit further down the power line road and found a beautiful spot with a fire ring and lots of open pines to string up a tarp. One ATV drove past earlier, and about an hour after I had set up, another camper Tacoma came by looking for a spot. I had a dip in the river to wash up, but the slope down to it is steep and a bit slippery. there&#39;s a nice shallow sand edge in the river though, and didn&#39;t find any leeches! good cell reception. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-04-29 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/233434 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
