 <wpt lat="46.883887" lon="-55.402323">
  <ele>8.286386187188327</ele>
  <time>2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Shoal Cove Beach</name>
  <desc>2 parking for any kind of RV.  The gravel road is not so bad, only the last 100m is rough but everyone can do it at low speed.&#xA;Nice view on Atlantic North Ocean and you can walk on the beach but for swimming it’s hazardous because dangerous undertow (there is a sign).&#xA;Some ATV came but there is a trail for them, just leave the entrance clear.&#xA;It’s locals that they encourage to stay there.&#xA;Before going there, the visit of the St. Lawrence Miner’s Museum worth the stop and why not have a good fish cake at the restaurant « Lunch Tin Cafe » 10-15h just in the same building of the museum.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/233690 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
