 <wpt lat="52.918545" lon="-111.232251">
  <ele>687.15135552641</ele>
  <time>2023-07-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Village of Irma Campground</name>
  <desc>Showers and washrooms are well maintained. The campground is at the north end of the village, right next to the Irma baseball diamonds so we watched a practice last night from out RV. It’s not the most gorgeous stop we’ve made but convenient right off Highway 881 and self registering so we could get in and back on the road quickly. There are picnic tables and a fire pit set up for cooking on each site. Many of the sites have water, sewer and hydro. &#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-07-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/234600 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
