 <wpt lat="47.667930" lon="-53.875480">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Rantem Station</name>
  <desc>This place is difficult to find. If you are traveling west, turn around at the exit to little harbor east. The access road is hard to see through the trees and it is beside a yield sign that can been seen driving westward. You will want to pull off to the shoulder before turning right and you definitely don&#39;t want to be making a left across the trans-Canada highway.&#xA;&#xA;The drive-able dirt road is short and stops by a pond. This is the location covered in an episode of the Newfoundland TV show &#34;Land and Sea&#34;.  You can park a Class A motorhome here and go fishing. The road continues, but you need an ATV or jeep as it is an old railway bed.&#xA;&#xA;If you look at the attached photos with the white Class B van, you can a small white sign. That sign is on the shoulder of the Trans Canada Highway.&#xA;&#xA;There is also a hill where you can drive a car and set up a tent. There are a few rock circles there from previous campfires.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/234650 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="50.120548" lon="-114.433444">
  <ele>1707.50253201928</ele>
  <time>2023-10-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>In a van down by the river</name>
  <desc>Lovely spot off 40, right next to the river. Hidden from the road and far enough to not get dusted or hear the cars going by. The other spots mentioned around here were full of RVs and trailers so I was looking for something only a self contained van or truck camper could make. This is perfect. No services, a nice place to disconnect. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/234697 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
