 <wpt lat="53.233531" lon="-105.086595">
  <ele>421.22271728515625</ele>
  <time>2023-09-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Saskatchewan River Forks Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Where the North and South forks of the Saskatchewan River meet. This isn&#39;t a formal campground but there are no signs prohibiting camping or staying overnight. The area is grassy with sand underneath, so wouldn&#39;t be a bad spot to pitch a tent. I wouldn&#39;t drive anything longer than 25 feet or 8 meters here. The trail to the river is officially closed but many people use it. The worst section is right at the top. I suggest long pants as there are some thorns and plenty of poison ivy, but it&#39;s not a bushwhack.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/235401 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#79d279</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="46.609746" lon="-73.061918">
  <ele>150.3</ele>
  <time>2023-09-22 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Lac Larose</name>
  <desc>Public Land accessible by trail. Be careful a lot of mountain bikes and motorcycles. It can also have party people but it&#39;s relatively quiet. The road is maintained by the city of St-Mathieu. Do not rely on Google map because it does not indicate any road. Follow road 724 towards Lac à la Coureuse then follow the indications towards Lac Larose.&#xA;---&#xA;Public Land accessible par la trail. Attention beaucoup de VTT et de moto. Il peut aussi avoir des fêtards mais c&#39;est relativement calme. La route est entretenu par la ville de st-mathieu. Ne pas se fier à Google map car il n&#39;indique aucune route. Suivre le chemin 724 vers lac à la coureuse puis suivre indications vers lac larose. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-22 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/235402 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
