 <wpt lat="52.969452" lon="-119.344777">
  <ele>785.978271484375</ele>
  <time>2024-06-28 04:25:17 UTC</time>
  <name>Stoneyard</name>
  <desc>We were recommended this area from our local White Water Rafting guide. It&#39;s an older gravel pit from when they built the road, but since has been abandoned. At first we didn&#39;t like the spot but it grew on us. There are all sorts of roads going to different spots with some being nicer then others. We still got a mountain view and the perfect amount of shade. Hike down to the river. Try to the find the abandoned Gold panning cabin!&#xA;&#xA;Definitely multiple big rig friendly with lots of turn around spots.&#xA;&#xA;(Follow the orange flags down to the river. Look for an overgrown walking path with and orange flag right by the last campsite before the road. take the overgrown road to the abandoned cabin)&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-28 04:25:17 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Bucket&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/235634 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
