 <wpt lat="48.769400" lon="-58.785220">
  <ele>2.964161992073059</ele>
  <time>2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>The Bar</name>
  <desc>The actual cottage town at the end on Highway 464 is “The Bar”, as it’s referred to by the locals. It’s a small fishing village used mostly during fishery seasons. This is not to be confused with the other two “The Bar” listings. As you drive down a 5-6 mile dirt road (potholes galore) you will pass a few spots that vehicles have used, both of which appear to be the other “The Bar” listings. I can’t speak to those, but I stayed at the very end of the drivable road after talking with a pair of locals…the dude whose front yard is adorned with oddities right before the start of the dirt road and who is one friendly guy and another guy who I let pass on the dirt road then actually waited for me to show me a moose. I asked about staying there and both said park anywhere. The fishing pier may stink, and the end of road is all-round beach stone compacted. Also, 1.5 miles further is a great walk to the navigation light. Worth the walk! Please future users, a great site. Don’t slob it up. It’s beautiful. Garbage place for the locals&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-24 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/235847 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
