 <wpt lat="60.016162" lon="-111.890422">
  <ele>145.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>By the Slave River </name>
  <desc>I drove around looking for a free spot out of town and came across this spot by the river. There is a natural boat ramp as well here. It was 930pm when I got here (still light during the summer). There are no signs anywhere saying overnight is not allowed. Around 10 p.m., RCMP drove by and did not stop or say anything to us. We are in a pop-up truck camper. The sound of the water is nice. There have been a couple of cars who have driven down here but nothing loud as of yet, and it is almost midnight (on a Wednesday). There is full cell service here, but no trash cans, toilets, or potable water. There are also no lights at all in this area.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/235940 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
