 <wpt lat="49.795987" lon="-118.714404">
  <ele>936.0581202544272</ele>
  <time>2023-08-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kettle River Crossing Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Wonderful small BC Forest Service recreation site with more than enough room to accommodate our tiny truck-house. There are two established sites on level ground but the one adjacent the river is the pick of the litter with the Kettle River and a sandy beach immediately below. Both sites have picnic benches, fire pits and there is public outhouse. It was nice enough for us to warrant spending 2 nights here.  Turn-off is 50 m past the bridge over the Kettle River at milepost “79 km below/down”.  More private and more room than the single campsite a kilometer or so down the road at “Sandy Beach”. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/236095 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
