  <ele>1461.664306640625</ele>
  <time>2023-08-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Bowles Evans forest service road, Mount Seven</name>
  <desc>Approx. halfway up Mount Seven just outside of Golden, BC. &#xA;Minor access road off main access tucked in to the right side. Flat camping spot with two rock fire pits. There are others in this area too. Road signs state forest access road not suitable for RVs but at time of visit was bumpy with some steep hairpin curves but fairly wide and accessible without extra ground clearance. The road is maintained well for the paragliding launch pad at the top. &#xA;Note: altitude is approximate estimate. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/236271 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
