 <wpt lat="46.323245" lon="-82.531512">
  <ele>237.00464947333677</ele>
  <time>2023-08-15 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Along McCarthy Lake Rd</name>
  <desc>The site is a pull-off of McCarthy Lake Rd ~1.5km from hwy 108. If you were crafty you could fit a small RV type unit in it, but it&#39;s more ideal for truck/car campers and tents. There is no cell service here for me (using T-Mobile), but we were able to use our satellite just off the back of the camp right beyond the tree line. Tree cover is available if you want it, but you can also park towards the edge of the spot nearer the road and get plenty of solar power. There&#39;s a clear fire ring and tent pad on the site. You&#39;re maybe a 1.5km walk to McCarthy Lake, and the site sits on a nice view of the marsh land leading to the lake (though it&#39;s elevated, so you&#39;re not all wet and soggy at camp). Not too much traffic on the road. Pretty and peaceful with plenty of space for our set up. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-15 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/236908 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
