 <wpt lat="44.143461" lon="-79.821019">
  <ele>187.280517578125</ele>
  <time>2023-08-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Geoff S. Gaston Park in Alliston Ontario.</name>
  <desc>very nice clean soccer parking lot with field. clean. lots of garbage cans, potty outhouses, and obviously a well maintained field and parking lot. unfortunately, we had to leave Earl Rowe Provincial Park after 1 night and couldn&#39;t find anything anywhere.  so we took our chances to come and crash rest here after ling exploring time and nothing available anywhere in this entire town, yet we all the way from Manitoba. it&#39;s dead here at 3 pm on a Saturday afternoon.  our dogs ran around a couple of local people who were here with their dogs. Keep the park clean, pick up your dogs stuff, and put it in the garbage disposal displayed. no fires here use your common sense and don&#39;t destroy a good stop place with nothing else in town here. there is a gate at the parks entrance, and the park can be found on Google. I guess no games nor big stuff going on. research why this park was created in 2017. kinda sad. but so peaceful and relaxing even to just come and hang here for the day. there us a sign on the road 500meters back says park open 5am to 11pm. but no signs displayed saying no overnight stopping or parking signs, however.  so I guess after talking with local people, you see lots boondocking here, yet no posting on it due to city bylaw. we also found nearby an old abandoned driveway by the corner light and could go there case we kicked out here our dogs enjoyed the race and run on the fields and catching Frisbee and the Ball. Be responsible and clean up, and NO fires also be respectful so others can come boondocking here for a night or couple since everything constantly is booked up in this area. Best time with relaxing and siltime here, no blasting music. be respectful to neighbors around. lots of room for big campers and turning. internet qith Telus 3 bars so good. Beautiful spot to come for a days away or as we did stay the night. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/237549 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
