 <wpt lat="47.614724" lon="-65.638558">
  <ele>7.037072422914207</ele>
  <time>2024-07-01 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Bathurst Lot</name>
  <desc>Dirt parking lot in secluded area on the Nepisiguit River. You will come to some parking lots on the way in that are not on the water - keep going!  Can drive into it however there are low hanging trees which may cause issues for taller vehicles. There is a large paved lot attached (great for tents) but dirt has been dumped on the entrance to prevent vehicle entry. Lots of room for turning.  Trash around indicates it is used by locals and saw tents here on a previous visit. Had a police visit in the evening (they we’re looking for someone specific). They had no issue when we said we were overnighting. Tim Hortons/Shell Gas combo stop with decent washrooms nearby (approximately 1/4 miles) for bathroom runs, coffee, and snacks. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-01 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/238489 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
