  <ele>85.6984674334526</ele>
  <time>2024-07-19 09:55:33 UTC</time>
  <name>Sir Richard Squires Memorial Prov. Park</name>
  <desc>This is a provincial park located on the Humber River. Note that Google maps may give you direction to take a dirt road from the Trans Canada Highway. Don&#39;t do this. The road in from Cormac is bad enough. Go slow or you will break your rig as it is one of the worst roads in Newfoundland.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-19 09:55:33 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Non-Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/238895 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
