 <wpt lat="49.078972" lon="-102.753132">
  <ele>526.3544578552246</ele>
  <time>2024-07-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Roche Percee Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>The campground is part of Roche Percee Provincial Park and difficult to find. Use the coordinates to get to it and find the sign. &#xA;As the place was flooded in 2011 and rebuilding is going on, there are only 14 very nice sites with tables and fireplaces. The other 30 will be opened over the year as the bridge collapsed connecting them. &#xA;For now there are only toilet houses, no showers and no water. But there’s a dump station. Charge is 20$ &#xA;There are a few seasonals as well but it was easy to find a spot end of August. &#xA;The historic site of Roche Percee is about 6km away&#xA;Usually you should book by calling 306-634-8101 or by email rocheperceepark@gmail.com. Payment is by e-transfer or if you&#39;re a dinosaur like me, just turn up and Kevin at site 4 can take cash and allocate you a site if available.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/238973 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
