  <time>2023-10-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Loon Lake Campground</name>
  <desc>Beautiful family oriented campground on a small lake just about 30 km from the USA border. Quiet, peaceful and clean. the road in was a little rough with some sharp corners but not to bad with our 1500 hauling our 28ft bumper pull travel trailer. Not sure a class A could navigate some of the turns but we did see one other bumper pull a little longer than ours set up in a site. plenty of sites available when we just showed up on Friday night of Labor day weekend. though the host did let us know it fills up on weekends in the summer, they have slowed down now bc kids are back in school. Host was very Kind Friendly and helpful. At only $14 CAN per night this was a perfect spot to stay before crossing back into the lower 48. Little to No service for internet with Verizon but texts were going through.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/239993 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
