 <wpt lat="45.427548" lon="-61.356055">
  <ele>6.748073577880859</ele>
  <time>2023-08-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Welsh Beach Road</name>
  <desc>Public dirt road that leads to a rocky beach. Spoke to one property owner at the end of the road who said people camp here frequently. No signs posted at all. The dirt road was surprisingly in good condition. Room for a van or two at the end of the road. We tent camped on the beach and had a bonfire. Only one person came by in the evening to fish for an hour. One or 2 cars drove in but turned around. Very peaceful. Once the clouds cleared at night the sky was full of stars. Bugs weren’t too bad either. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/240817 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
