  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="52.701670" lon="-119.189804">
  <ele>2150.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Canoe Mountain Alpine</name>
  <desc>A beautiful spot on the west side of Canoe Mountain. There are no facilities here, just a beautiful view and some trees to protect from the wind. This spot is only accessible from mid to late Summer when it and the road is free of snow. It is located on Crown Land and is open to anyone.&#xA;&#xA;Canoe Mountain Road is very rocky and requires a vehicle with low range gearing, with reasonably high clearance. This is not a road for a mall-crawling SUV. It is best to put the vehicle in low range right when leaving the highway as the entire trail is up hill until the alpine, with an average grade of 14%. It takes about an hour to reach the top of the mountain or the camping spot.&#xA;&#xA;At the alpine, the camping spot is located on the side trail that heads south from the weather station.&#xA;&#xA;Cell reception is spotty, but there is good reception on top of the mountain. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/240902 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
