 <wpt lat="50.046122" lon="-125.306579">
  <ele>15.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Gravel Lot under Power Lines</name>
  <desc>Traveling beyond the two linked nearby points, you turn left on Iron River Rd. At this point, you enter a dirt road that becomes quite rough with deep ruts and potholes. We went slow in our 2WD low clearance van and did fine. About 1 km in, you reach the clearing for power lines and turn left on a gravel drive in. This area is large with lots of room to set up and turn around. Nice view of the mountain range. &#xA;&#xA;This is a spot for locals as well. Unfortunately, lots of garbage left behind including pizza boxes, blankets, and a dead cat :( Locals drive the road quick in pick ups, and there was a dirt biker that came through via the hiking trail. Not sure I’d recommend any more than 1-2 nights based on this, but no one bothered us. &#xA;&#xA;Also an active bear area with fresh scat on the road in. And we rustled something awake in the morning that was sleeping veryyyyy close to our site. Most likely a bear, but there are also cougars in the area. &#xA;&#xA;Please leave no trace! &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/241213 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
