 <wpt lat="51.418817" lon="-112.889784">
  <ele>855.0</ele>
  <time>2024-06-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Horseshoe canyon natural area</name>
  <desc>There are NO signs here saying &#34;no overnight parking,&#34; like there are at the Horseshoe Canyon Hiking trail entrance.The main sign (attached) says it is &#34;privately owned&#34;, and &#34;visitors use these premises at their own risk&#34;. This is a primitive parking area in a field on a loop. There are no restrooms or trashcans here, but you can just walk over to the other lot if you need those. There is also open wifi on that other area, but not here. Had no issues, and there was one other vehicle here. Please keep this place clean and do not abuse it. Added photos. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/241352 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
