 <wpt lat="60.113019" lon="-130.683565">
  <ele>681.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-01 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Rancheria Radio Tower Road</name>
  <desc>Well established road leaves the Alaska Highway and climbs steeply to a radio tower site at the summit of a small mountain. There is a turn around and well protected camp site near the base of the mountain. Small RV&#39;s could go this far. Trucks or high clearance vehicles can make it to the top. There are no turn around options once you start up the road until you get to the top, and some sections are steep. At the top are great views and space for several vehicles to park, though the wind noise through the tower can be loud. A 4x4 trail leaves the top and continues for many kilometers in the alpine, with excellent camp sites along it mostly used by hunters in the fall. We easily found space for 2 trucks 30 seconds down the 4x4 trail. Please be gentle on the alpine vegetation!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-01 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/241366 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="44.587288" lon="-79.682701">
  <ele>148.63790509190218</ele>
  <time>2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Copland forest</name>
  <desc>Copland forest trail parking (P2). No &#34;no overnight parking&#34; sign. no toilet, no amenities. relatively calm, we heard one train passing at night and the road is calm at night. several places for RVs but no big rigs as access and road are narrow. I would not stay several nights as there is a lumber company and an habitation across the road, to not attract attention.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/241399 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
