 <wpt lat="51.469873" lon="-120.534933">
  <ele>1115.3009033203125</ele>
  <time>2023-08-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Lake Access next to Cove Resort</name>
  <desc>On the intersection that leads to &#34;Cove Resort&#34; turn left to find two flat spots for camping. It&#39;s close to the highway that was quite frequented by trucks on a night Sunday to Monday but should be fine with earplugs. You have a beautiful view on Lac des Roches and even access to it. Seems to be in use as there are old fire pits all around. Would recommend only overnighters as the lake Access seems to be used as well. But aside from that I was totally undisturbed. &#xA;Further down there is a forest road and some kind of &#34;wildlife crossing tunnel&#34; beneath the highway, so maybe not camp right in front of it.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/241594 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
