 <wpt lat="51.197742" lon="-116.621560">
  <ele>1150.9024609420449</ele>
  <time>2024-07-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Forest Road </name>
  <desc>This is a hidden gem! Secluded spot down an old logging road that is accessible by most vehicles as long as it doesn’t get super rutted from the rain. Not suitable for long trailers or RVs due to the narrow winding road. You have wonderful Mountain views and the space all to yourself, no other spots down the road for at least 1/2 mile (I didn’t drive further). Could fit several cars or small rigs here. Lots of mosquitos like everywhere else, and about 30-45 mins from Yoho NP and some good hikes. There’s also a waterfall trail right down the road that I didn’t check out. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/241850 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
