  <name>Rosebud Valley Campground</name>
  <desc>Town-owned campground in the town of Didsbury, Alberta. Most sites have power, some 15 amp, many 30 amp. Some have water. There is no dump station at the campground, but the town has one 5 minutes away. Most sites are a good size, but there are no trees between them. Managers are very nice to deal with.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/241942 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
