 <wpt lat="54.292935" lon="-116.210511">
  <ele>886.6429248994037</ele>
  <time>2023-09-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Virginia Hills Rest Area</name>
  <desc>A rest stop on the northbound side of the highway. Many of them along this highway. There are toilets and rubbish bins but google reviews indicate the toilets are not good (we didn&#39;t try). There&#39;s a better reviewed rest area on the southbound side of the highway further south if you&#39;re heading that way. Trucks pull in and out throughout the night but far enough from the highway to not be too noisy. Spent one night no problem. No signs saying you can&#39;t stay overnight and googled to see if there were any prohibitions in general in Alberta and found nothing.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/242255 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
