 <wpt lat="46.799022" lon="-71.217425">
  <ele>4.593673293161016</ele>
  <time>2024-05-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Champlain Street</name>
  <desc>Nice one-way street to camp up.  Narrow street, not for big rigs.  Quiet at night.  Can essentially park along here between 7pm and 9am and with the 1 hour free parking that could stretch 6pm to 10am.  The further along you go, the closer walk it is to Old Quebec.  Fantastic place from which to visit the City.  When you have to leave by 10am, you can park at the parking at Sapear Street.  Here it is 4 hours of free parking (but no overnight parking) and there are washrooms if needs be as well as right on the river and parkway.  Looking back up the hill are  the steps leading up to the Plains of Abraham. We walked up through the town, up to the Chateau and boulevard, up to the Plains and down the stairs.  Wonderful.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Fast&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/242540 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
