 <wpt lat="48.947666" lon="-66.125618">
  <ele>-26.0</ele>
  <time>2023-09-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Camping de la Rivière </name>
  <desc>Large sites but not a lot of privacy. No cell service but Wifi available at the road (not at your site). The gîte up the road has a nice restaurant. Unfortunately Quebec had a weird dislike of dogs, so this was the only campground in the provincial park that allowed them, and there was only one boring trail that we could take our dog on. This could be a great park if you are looking to disconnect, but if you have a dog I would avoid it.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: No&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/242748 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
