 <wpt lat="49.490463" lon="-56.074742">
  <ele>5.581449723802507</ele>
  <time>2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Indian River Walking Trailhead</name>
  <desc>The parking lot is at the end of Main Street. Be careful of the steep incline of the entrance. The gravel lot is large and flat enough for two or three rigs. Very quiet site to spend the night and no signs prohibiting staying. A beautiful, well-maintained boardwalk to hike the wetlands. There’s interpretive signage along the way and at the trail head. Garbage containers but no other facilities. A lovely, picturesque spot.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Fast&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/242893 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
