 <wpt lat="51.271627" lon="-80.640143">
  <ele>10.223629062995315</ele>
  <time>2023-09-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Riverfront, Moosonee </name>
  <desc>There is a small gravel Carpark right by the river. It’s level. There are great views over the river and sandbar to the island. There’s a path and picnic shelters nearby so you get a bit of noise from passers-by. And you cause a lot of interest as there have been very few people camping here before- so expect people stopping to talk to you. Access is via the Polar Bear Express train , 5 hours from Cochrane. They check the size of your rig to see if they will allow it on the train. They allowed our Pop top truck camper on at the normal rate for cars. You can’t drive hardly anywhere here so the only advantage is that you can sleep and eat for free. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/243217 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
