  <name>Quiet alternative to nearby camp</name>
  <desc>A lovely hidden spot just off the road towards Kinuseo Falls. It is basically an overgrown gravel spot next to a creek and forest. The overgrowth might make turning around with a big camper challenging but for us with a small car and tent it was ideal. Also has a fire ring and plenty of fresh water from the creek. No cars at night or in the morning. H+ signal so could look up some things as well.&#xA;&#xA;We originally planned to stay at the marked campsite 5min from here but the noise from the overhead electrical lines was too loud and the best spot was taken by someone who looked like he was going to stay for a while.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-29 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/243978 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
