 <wpt lat="46.747056" lon="-83.980561">
  <ele>297.4970703125</ele>
  <time>2023-09-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>past Searchmont on 556 - Ranger Rd</name>
  <desc>A reclaimed gravel pit.  3 established fire rings with plenty of room for a couple of larger rigs.  There&#39;s a creek just down a short atv trail.  The trail crosses the creek and continues.  I stayed 3 nights only had 2 vehicles pull in to check it out and 1 atv drive through the trail.   You can hear the infequent traffic pass on the 556   &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/244299 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="48.651083" lon="-124.592722">
  <ele>192.8</ele>
  <time>2023-09-28 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Central Walbran campsite</name>
  <desc>Informal campground just prior to bridge with a few additional tenting sites on the west side where the trailheads to several Walbran trails start. Two small shelters to keep dry. One has a wood stove and wood. Also a few outhouses, one on each side of the river. Only smaller vehicle access; suggest 4x4 or awd. Have to cross one narrow landslide area and road is somewhat brushy. &#xA;We did the hike into Anderson Lake. There’s no longer a cable car so expect to cross the river and one creek on foot. Would not cross during spring runoff! The upper crossing is a log jamb which we missed on the way in. Watch for small wood sign ~150 m past Maxine’s Tree that doubles back downstream to the crossing. Trail is mostly flat with only one short steep section. Forest very beautiful with lots of massive spruce, hemlock and cedar vets. Anderson Lake is very pretty but doesn’t have beaches or fish by the looks of it. We left just prior to a micology workshop which is an annual event and likely uses most/all the campsites. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-28 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/244320 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="48.458086" lon="-124.062035">
  <ele>460.23558690585196</ele>
  <time>2023-09-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Jordan North Main ~3.5km</name>
  <desc> Fantastic little spot at the end of a spur road into a recently logged 2023 cutblock. Two flat spots with room for tents or pickups with campers. Nice view of the ocean and very sunny which is great in the fall and for the solar panels. Also away from the dusty FSR traffic. No shade or water if it’s hot. Peaceful with the sound of the creek off in the distance. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/244321 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="47.662410" lon="-70.777890">
  <ele>710.0</ele>
  <time>2023-08-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Arthabaska Campground</name>
  <desc>Stunning campground in Parc national des Grands-Jardins. All excellent camp sites that can accommodate tents, RVs and trailers (except a few walk-in camp sites). All gravel and level. (Sometimes impossible to peg into ground, but ability to guy to trees. No services. Free showers and plumbed toilets, plus some pit toilets. Many sites offer great views of the surrounding hills/mountains. The entire park is covered with blueberry bushes that were perfectly ripe when we visited (mid-August) and it’s allowed to pick the blueberries for personal/immediate consumption. Excellent hiking from the campground, as well as the ability to rent canoes/kayaks/SUP for exploring Lake Arthabaska and river network. The other sector of the park offers serviced camp sites (although in a less stunning location), as well as more hiking and via ferrata (recommended!). No cellular signal, but free (decent) wifi available at the visitors centre, which appears to be powered by Starlink.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-08-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: No&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/244358 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
