  <ele>23.0</ele>
  <time>2023-10-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Roosevelt Campobello International Park</name>
  <desc>While chatting with the visitor center staff they mentioned you could stay in their parking lot overnight for no cost after the CG closes for the season. There were three staff members there when the information was shared. &#xA;&#xA;I did not stay here or ask about check-in procedures but figured it was noteworthy enough to share. I ended up riding my bike from the US across the bridge. &#xA;&#xA;Really cool park site with free tours. Try to schedule in advance for the twice daily and free Tea With Eleanor. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-10-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/245848 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
