 <wpt lat="49.533833" lon="-124.709954">
  <ele>14.276884497143328</ele>
  <time>2023-12-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Bradsdadsland Campground</name>
  <desc>Decent sized campground close to the ferry dock on Hornby Island. Sites are quite small but have picnic tables and fire pits. We came in December, so no services (no power, or sewer), but there was potable water. I think they do offer power in the summer months (as there was a power box on my site, but not working). Great view of ocean from several sites, some road noise as it’s right on the main island road. Very quiet at night though. They do have laundry (machines are old and dryers are not great) - $2.25 to wash and $2 for 50 min dryer time. Hot showers ($1/2min) and flush toilets are available. There are very few options on this island for accommodations, so this was a necessary stop, but I felt the $45 fee was way overpriced for having no power. Only stayed one night because too expensive. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-12-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - Not at Sites&#xA;Wifi: Unknown&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/252239 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
