 <wpt lat="45.729819" lon="-73.639945">
  <ele>17.69</ele>
  <time>2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Parc Des Saules. Mascouche</name>
  <desc>Gravel parking between a beautiful park and an ancestral cemetery. Located 7 min off highway 640. Overnight parking is not allowed directly at the park but if you don&#39;t cross the fence, you can stay at the cemetary parking.  Dogs are not allowed in the park but there is no problem for the cemetary.  There is a wood you can walk through, a baseball field, picnic tables and many games for kids.  It is clean and beautiful.  There is a small water fountain only for small bottle, not accessible with a vehicle and closed during winter.  I slept there 3 nights but not in a row and nobody bothered me.  There is recycle bin but no garbage bin.  Cell phone is perfect.  Place is very quiet.  The parking can hold maybe 25 cars or 3 big rigs.  The park parking is used as a hockey skating ring. This morning maybe 100 small children came to play.   Keep in mind that the cemetery is separate from the park.  There is houses pretty close but I did not feel shy at all.  For big rigs, it could be tricky to go there since you have to go through a residential neighborhood.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/263589 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
