 <wpt lat="45.979600" lon="-67.240519">
  <ele>31.325151031836867</ele>
  <time>2024-03-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Nackawic Nature Trail Parking Lot</name>
  <desc>Parking lot situated at the south end of the 2km trail (to the world&#39;s biggest axe in Nackawic). Near the Big Axe brewery, which was closed when we drove by. No amenities on site or nearby. The place is big enough for several cars/minivans or 1-2 RV&#39;s, but only the bottom part is leveled. There were no signs prohibiting overnight parking or camping (the trail is on Crown land itself). We had dinner and stayed the night without any problems. Quiet place, just a few cars passing by (or locals going for a walk with their dog on the trail) but we didn&#39;t hear much inside our van. Nice view on the river as a bonus!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-03-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/267177 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
