 <wpt lat="46.821574" lon="-66.642622">
  <ele>-1.0</ele>
  <time>2024-04-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Lay-by close to river on 108</name>
  <desc>We found this small lay-by that had been cleared from snow, which saved us for a night, given the other places on this app were situated on inaccessible dirt roads at this time of year. This one could be a turnaround point, and also leads to a kind of refuge, closed when we came. Quiet night, very few vehicles drove by. No services at all, not even cell. No signs prohibiting parking. Space for several cars, maybe 1 or 2 bigger rigs. Okay for an &#34;emergency&#34; stop.&#xA;&#xA;Important note: we recommend avoiding the 108 if you have a trailer or questionable suspensions... It&#39;s in very bad condition with potholes, bumps everywhere! If your car can handle it, it&#39;s a beautiful drive though :) &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-04-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/269240 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
