 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="46.250708" lon="-63.693953">
  <ele>6.763819989748299</ele>
  <time>2024-07-02 20:52:47 UTC</time>
  <name>Next to port borden front range lighthouse</name>
  <desc>Found this place while walking around to check the lighthouse. I parked here with my small travel trailer to stay the night. TONS of mosquitoes but it beats sleeping in a parking lot. There is room for a medium side travel trailer and medium rig to turn around. The gravel road to access this place is right on front of street address &#34;227 carleton street&#34;. In front there is a Gravel road right next to &#34;harbourview lane&#34; which goes to the decommissioned lighthouse. There is a big grassy area next to the lighthouse and antena where you can park for the night. Very quiet. No prohibition signs. small 4x4 could keep going on the grassy road and park along the cliff. 4x4 needed to go further down the road passed the lighthouse due to muddy potholes. cool spot!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-02 20:52:47 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/272620 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
