 <wpt lat="50.919603" lon="-114.050436">
  <ele>1022.7126319774122</ele>
  <time>2024-05-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Quiet Street by Fish Creek Provincial Park</name>
  <desc>Street parking along this curved street with Fish Creek Provincial Park on one side and condos on the other. I&#39;d say vans only, I think RVs would probably attract too much attention as there are a lot of people walking their dogs. Planet Fitness is close. I couldn&#39;t find a better place in Calgary so returned three nights after leaving during the day. There&#39;s a bus stop at the end of the curve on the  street that goes to the train station to go downtown but I drove to the nearest Park and Ride lot so as not to leave my van here all day and attract more attention. No toilets or trash bins. I&#39;m not sure if any trails go into the park from here as it was raining and cold so I didn&#39;t explore. I only had 1-2 bars with Google Fi but it worked well enough to watch YouTube. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/273042 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
