 <wpt lat="64.020350" lon="-139.145680">
  <ele>353.8</ele>
  <time>2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Beaver dam at Hunker Creek</name>
  <desc>Gravel area close to a 🦫 beaver dam, maybe made of mine debris. Flat open area, for 3-4 RVs max. &#xA;Access just in front if the wooden mine tower. Access may be not suitable for big RVs.&#xA;There are 2 ponds connected by the dam. We saw 5 beavers and the site is plenty of moose footprints. Nice view on the sunset between the mountains. Few to none mosquitos.&#xA;Vehicles driving on the close-by gravel road are visible, however, it’s overall very quiet.&#xA;We stayed 2 nights, while visiting Dawson City and hiking.&#xA;No facilities. Verizon 3/5&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/273456 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.595870" lon="-121.929376">
  <ele>13.64932834192156</ele>
  <time>2023-09-19 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Kirkland Creek Recreation Reserve</name>
  <desc>From Sts’ailes Forest Road, less then half mile, to Harrison Lake lakeshore.&#xA;The access is in a beautiful rain forest, to a wide and flat open space with a fire ring and several fire pits.&#xA;Camp options are: in the open area for big RVs or trailers, in the forest for tents, on the pebble lakeshore for 4x4, where there is a Canadian flag and a swing. We stayed 1 night on the lakeshore: the view is gorgeous, the only sound was by the waves on the pebbles.&#xA;The location is truly lovely, however, spoiled by garbage: aluminum cans, plastic bottles, plastic cutlery, napkins, big cardboard boxes. Toilet paper everywhere!&#xA;Please LEAVE NO TRACE!&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2023-09-19 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/273458 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="50.724563" lon="-113.967067">
  <ele>1041.0459862453863</ele>
  <time>2024-05-11 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Street Parking</name>
  <desc>Parked in a quiet residential area in Okotoks.  Enjoyed a quiet night’s sleep.  A field across the street for walking your dogs.  Within walking distance to the historic centre of Okotoks with its restaurants, pubs and shopping.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-11 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/273475 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
