 <wpt lat="49.801740" lon="-125.163054">
  <ele>73.05938720703125</ele>
  <time>2024-05-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Huge Pullout on HWY 19S</name>
  <desc>Long Pullover Site for Tired Drivers, Trucks, Etc. No toilets or amenities. I was traveling South from North Vancouver Island. Approximately 6 km South of Hamm Rd Exit I noticed a transport truck parked here. it was 3 a.m. and I was tired. My Grand Caravan is 2 front seats and a bed. I slept from 3 a.m. until noon. No problems no hassles. It was just me when I woke up. I slept well. &#xA;No street lights so keep a sharp eye. &#xA;virtually no traffic at night. 3 bars on my device. I was able to reserve a ferry to Vancouver (from Nanaimo) at 3am using my device. &#xA;3 images attached. Everything to the right of the sign (see pic) is fair game for parking. Note: I  have a 3L heavy duty urinal, but the dense woods would work in a pinch. &#xA;Keep it safe. Park to the Right of the Faded White Line. Peace from BC. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/273813 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="49.420963" lon="-107.074984">
  <ele>721.4290210390463</ele>
  <time>2024-05-13 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Grasslands Inn Hotel &amp; Restaurant</name>
  <desc>As there were almost no registered spot in the area between the two blocs of Grasslands NP, we asked the waitress (owner?) of the local hotel if it would be possible to stay in the parking lot for the night, after having a drink at the hotel’s bar. She said no problem. We did so, parked behind the building and had a great night. &#xA;&#xA;The bar is really not fancy (very little choice of beers, no cider, no wine by the glass…) but does the job. We ordered curly fries that were really good. We did not order anything else but the restaurant has good reviews on Gmaps. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-13 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Unknown&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/273818 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
