 <wpt lat="45.350089" lon="-73.262931">
  <ele>15.2</ele>
  <time>2024-06-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Parc Dacquier Parking</name>
  <desc>Very Nice spot for short term or overnight situated alongside the Chambly Canal in St.Jean sur Richelieux. Beutifull place to take a walk or bike ride along the canal. No signage indicating restrictions. Not a large Parking but can easily hold a few small RV&#39;s or 2 Long Rv&#39;s One Toilet, Picnic tables and plenty of garbage cans. Quiet place but lots of people daytime for lunch and walks. &#xA;There&#39;s a Restaurant called Chez Menoncle right across the canal. I stayed overnight with my 35f RV. Parked in the back corner and no issues. Police passed 3 times without even a look. &#xA;Keep in mind that This is a park so no camping or fires. keep it clean and respect others.&#xA;Good luck and happy VanLife!&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Unknown&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: Yes&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/274519 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
