  <desc>Locks on the Tay Canal run by Parks Canada. Super friendly staff that say “just park wherever you want”. Told me it was $5.50 per night per person then said don’t worry about it. Got a great spot for the night with electricity for nothing. The scenery is spectacular. Might only operate from May to October. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-05-25 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Fast&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/275391 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
