  <time>2024-06-26 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Road off Trans-Canada Highway</name>
  <desc>An old highway that has been overgrown with plantlife but is still drivable. It&#39;s right beside the highway. There is a big pothole near the beginning that needs to be carefully driven around, but I got around it with my small car. Would be a good place to stop and sleep for the night.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/277100 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
