 <wpt lat="49.385211" lon="-121.473618">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Landstrom Ridge Trailhead</name>
  <desc>This is adjacent to a weigh scale and Google labels it as a trailhead. I pulled in at 11pm. Located next to tracks and heard train go by at 11 and 11:30pm. Not sure if there were any later as I am a hard sleeper. The scale was closed so it was easy to slide in. No facilities but has the rest stop feel due to its proximity to the road. Woke up at 7:30am and the scale was open. I quick walked the dogs then boogied out of there.&#xA;I travel in my car but this is large enough for a trailer. Just make sure your Back-up game is solid. &#xA;Fairly level. Two bars for Verizon.&#xA;Hope, BC is less than 10 min away.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Average&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/277843 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="48.592328" lon="-124.263209">
  <ele>13.97943584062159</ele>
  <time>2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Harris creek free wild camps</name>
  <desc>Severals spots with fire pits in the Forest. &#xA;Four for cars/RV/campers and others for tents or walkers. The last big one spot is at the end of the road.&#xA;Road on grown/gravel (contratry to the other spot on Harris creek) No need 4x4, OK with classic car. &#xA;Easy access to the river, clean and clear. &#xA;No garbage, Please pack it what you bring, the place is very clean.&#xA;Kind of handcrafted pit toilet next to the river, around the second spot.&#xA;Hidden, quiet and not to close from the road. &#xA;When you come from Port Renfrew, turn on the right just AFTER the bridge. &#xA;When you come from Cowichan, turn on the left BEFORE the bridge.&#xA;Cell service slow (Rogers)&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-10 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/277867 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
