 <wpt lat="45.863690" lon="-76.739470">
  <ele></ele>
  <time>2024-06-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Pont Felix Gabriel Marchand Bridge</name>
  <desc>This space is part of the Route 148 circuit in Pontiac, which includes some twenty RV stops, some of which are free. &#xA;&#xA;This 1898 construction is the longest covered bridge in Quebec. Thanks to citizen participation, since its renovation in 2022, it has been fitted with thousands of coloured lights that illuminate it in the evening. With the app, you can even change the colors!&#xA;&#xA;RV rest area for motorized Class B only&#xA;&#xA;To access the restrooms and picnic tables, simply head for the Halte de Plein Air. As space is limited, we ask you to respect the designated RV parking areas. The RV Stop is located near the ball field. You&#39;re invited to join in community, cultural and sporting events. On site, you can also fish along the Coulonge River with the proper permits, or enjoy the PPJ bike path and nearby Bryson House.&#xA;&#xA;This site is free and open year round.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/279459 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
