 <wpt lat="47.982229" lon="-66.233574">
  <ele>3.514694911427796</ele>
  <time>2024-07-03 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>West side of the peninsula</name>
  <desc>Wow what a great spot if you have SUV  or pickup truck.  This is not for a big rig or even RV.    What a beautiful view, the West side is exposed to the wind so less bugs. Much nicer than the east side.  The parking spot is at the end of the trail straight ahead. It is between two cottages that are about 100 metres away on each side.  There’s a lot of spruces and moose tracks here.  You can’t see the cottages unless you walk and follow the shore at low tide    We camped here only one night.    Wish we had more time.   It is a rocky beach. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-03 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/279635 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
