   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
 <wpt lat="61.333331" lon="-122.094335">
  <ele>180.40789759345353</ele>
  <time>2024-06-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Birch Creek Side Road - 2 locations</name>
  <desc>The one closest to the main road (75 yards) is relatively flat, has an unofficial location for fires, and you can hear the creek which is only 30 ft away.  Can walk down to Birch Creek pretty easily.  Mostly surrounded by trees.  Quite pretty (except the black flies).  There is one spot down further away from the road that you can see the creek. It is prettier but has deep ruts from tires and could get stuck if rained on.  Some low hanging small trees on side of road.  Very nice and open down there, but a little risky for 2WD tall Transit van (we have been stuck before so we may be a little more conservative). &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/279648 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
