  <name>Near entrance to Cape St. Mary&#39;s Ecological Reserve </name>
  <desc>This is a large flat pullout near the basement remains of an old building, but otherwise nothing nearby. It is just west of the entrance road to Cape St. Mary&#39;s Ecological Reserve, across from a blue sign for the Reserve.&#xA;&#xA;Traffic was sparse all night.&#xA;&#xA;Smaller vehicles can pull further from the road, but there is plenty of room for a few rigs parallel to the road&#xA;&#xA;Cell service is intermittent, but almost none so don&#39;t count on it.&#xA;&#xA;Recommended also as day parking for large rigs (with toads) as the entrance road is two lanes, but very thin.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-26 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/280445 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
