 <wpt lat="48.518480" lon="-64.246621">
  <ele>281.21215965219244</ele>
  <time>2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>trail head - Sentier des Montagnes </name>
  <desc>Great spot at the trail head. Quick easy ride up the hill from town. You first arrive at a paved parking spot with an abandoned house. You could stay there but there was a lot of trash and broken glass so we kept going up the dirt road to the left. There is a left spur that goes to a large clearing with several fire pits, but no view. We kept going to the trailhead and from here we have a really nice view of the valley and the water below! There is a small firepit here as well. Room for 2 vans, but only one spot will have the view! You can also keep going another 100 ft and there is a large clearing by the cell tower (some tall tower, whatever it is). No water view but it would do if you needed another spot. It was very windy all night, van was shaking, but it had been very windy all day, even in town. and the fog rolled in so we lost our view the following morning. But lots of wild flowers around so still a beautiful quiet place to spend the night.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-06-30 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/281085 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#00ff00</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
