 <wpt lat="57.984082" lon="-130.078075">
  <ele>907.1988462935136</ele>
  <time>2024-07-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Morchuea Lake Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Super nice campsite with pit toilets and some tables. There are quite a few sites for campers of all sizes, strewn around and nicely spaced. The view of the lake and the mountains in the background is amazing, for example at sunset. (no camp spot right at the waterfront though, you&#39;ll have to walk ~50m) We stayed here one night and it was very calm, surprisingly few people for such a nice place. You can sometimes hear loud trucks passing by on the road but not the normal cars. The road down is somewhat bumpy but probably doable in normal 2WDs.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/281143 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
