 <wpt lat="55.116577" lon="-105.245633">
  <ele>382.36841583251953</ele>
  <time>2024-07-02 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Nut Point Campground</name>
  <desc>A busy little campground right next to La Ronge. Approx 90 sites, some powered, some not. Potable water on site as well as dump station, boat launch, free firewood, pit toilets, flush toilets and free showers. This place basically hasn’t been updated since built - shower stalls are tiny with no hooks, but pressure is good and it’s free, so no real complaints there. $20/night for no power, $33/night for power. Must reserve online as no one appears to work in the booth on site, and in doing so, there is an $11 reservation fee - doesn’t look like there is any way around that. Some sites are tiny and sloped, some are large and level and some have great views and access of Lac La Ronge. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-02 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/281573 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
  </extensions>
 </wpt>
