 <wpt lat="45.725230" lon="-74.261020">
  <ele></ele>
  <time>2024-07-04 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Lake Beattie Nature Park</name>
  <desc>The Lake Beattie Nature Park is 300 Hectars and has 4 vanlife spaces. The park includes 20 km of trails and a beautiful lake where you can bring your kayak, canoe or paddleboard. No motors on the lake. The rate for a vanlife space is $20/night and DOES NOT INCLUDE park access fees which will be charged to you upon arrival if you have not included them in the payment of your reservation. reservation can be made online here : https://reservotron.com/municipalite-du-canton-de-gore?c=198260.  If you are an annual member, you do not have to pay access fees.&#xA;&#xA;The Vanlife space is made for you if:&#xA;&#xA;    your VEHICLE is 25 feet or less.&#xA;    you only have ONE vehicle/site.&#xA;    you DO NOT HAVE a ROAD EQUIPMENT (vehicle + trailer prohibited)&#xA;    you are 100% autonomous, zero waste. (sites without service)&#xA;&#xA;the Vanlife space (4 places) is located in a wooded parking lot, right on the trails and very close to the lake (around 500m). It is the ideal place to relax and enjoy nature. The VanLife space has a common area with picnic tables and a fire pit (wood on sale at Reception).&#xA;&#xA;Not included:&#xA;&#xA;    Running water (drinking water on sale at reception)&#xA;    Electricity&#xA;    Sanitary block (dry toilet nearby)&#xA;    wood for the campfire&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-04 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Unknown&#xA;Wifi: Unknown&#xA;Kitchen: Unknown&#xA;Restaurant: Unknown&#xA;Showers: Unknown&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Unknown&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/281862 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
   <osmand:amenity_subtype>user_defined_other_postcode</osmand:amenity_subtype>
   <osmand:amenity_type>user_defined_other</osmand:amenity_type>
