 <wpt lat="53.257668" lon="-121.408045">
  <ele>904.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Bowron Lake Lodge Campground</name>
  <desc>The Campground has many site direct at the bowron lake. You can walk just a few metres from your site into the water. It&#39;s the only campground at Bowron Lake. The provencial park campground is in the forest.&#xA;It could be a little bit crowded at the water in the Summer at the weekends. &#xA;It&#39;s 47,25$ per night including taxes.&#xA;The showers are old, but you can take a bath in the lake. It&#39;s a great spot after the Bowron Lake Circuit. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Warm&#xA;Water: Unknown&#xA;Toilets: Unknown&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/282547 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
