 <wpt lat="45.359646" lon="-65.524208">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Cliff above sea caves</name>
  <desc>A quiet campsite on the cliff above the sea caves and view of the St Martins Bay. There is enough room for a couple camper vans or smaller vehicles. I would not recommend this for a larger rig because of the tight turnaround right at the edge of the cliff. It is hard to find a totally flat spot but workable. There was already a small fire pit and sadly some trash. Seems like the spot the local teens come to drink, but we did not have any rowdy teens come by that night and it was Canada Day. A really nice local couple walked over to watch the sunset and did not say anything to discourage camping. Great launching spot for the Fundy Trail Parkway. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-23 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/282548 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
