 <wpt lat="53.710927" lon="-105.942509">
  <ele>530.5111599694937</ele>
  <time>2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Anderson Point - Anglin Lake</name>
  <desc>Delightful campground on Anglin Lake. Approx 60 sites, most are quite private and large. All sites have power, and are $33/night. As with all Provincial Parks, you must also have a park pass. No onsite registration, must be done by phone or online, with a $11.50 reservation fee tacked on. Free showers, free firewood, nice trail through campground, beach, playground and boat launch. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-07 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: Yes - At Sites&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: Hot&#xA;Water: Potable&#xA;Toilets: Running Water&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/282613 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Established Campground</type>
  <extensions>
   <osmand:icon>tourism_camp_site</osmand:icon>
   <osmand:background>circle</osmand:background>
   <osmand:color>#339933</osmand:color>
