 <wpt lat="51.264660" lon="-116.747211">
  <ele>986.7460068389773</ele>
  <time>2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Right next to the Kicking horse </name>
  <desc>Great beautiful spot right on the river. We got our 31ft motorhome down here without an issue. The ground is solid packed gravel. I have seen school buses hauling river rafts in and out of the water without any problems. &#xA;&#xA;We stayed here 5 nights. I recommend carry bear spray if you decide to camp here. We saw a good sized black bear with the her cub came out of the woods and having a stroll along the river bank on our 3rd day. The view at sunset is beautiful. Lots of woods available for camp fire. You can hear the trains occasionally. It didn’t bother us. Overall great experience.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/282675 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
