 <wpt lat="47.811739" lon="-64.537285">
  <ele>-11.896575927734375</ele>
  <time>2024-07-08 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Cap Bateau off road</name>
  <desc>Right after you pass the village, there is a curvy going to the left, on the right at the end of the curvy there is a dirt road that takes you to 2 small dirt &#34;parkings&#34;. enough room for a few small campers or 1-2 medium rigs. This ground is not that much leveled but it&#39;s worth sleeping crooked for a night. right on the Ocean. very nice spots to check out. very quiet. I did not sleep here. this place was recommended by my boondocking host who lives in Lamèque. the picture I took of the parking area didn&#39;t save on my phone. I recommend for sleeping :). bring vinegar! there are jellyfishes a lot around the islands.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-08 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/282792 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
