 <wpt lat="52.479474" lon="-113.445293">
  <ele>846.0977439880371</ele>
  <time>2024-07-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Clive municipal campground</name>
  <desc>Six back-in sites on east side (to the right) of the ball diamond. Drive through the gate at the north end of 49 St. Sites are big enough for our 32’ RV, grassy enough for tents. No services. Sites are close together but there are mature trees between sites for privacy.  We were the only ones here in peak camping season. Fee of $5 payable to municipality, but nobody came by to collect.  Bonus: watch a free baseball game on the diamond. There is a municipal trailer dump station just a few blocks away. &#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: Yes - Slow&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/282808 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
