 <wpt lat="44.721547" lon="-65.007351">
  <ele>184.98311408054033</ele>
  <time>2024-07-09 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Shannon River Canoe Access Park</name>
  <desc>Beautiful small gravel lot right off the road. Doesn’t seem to be enough room for a big rig to turn around and wouldn’t recommend more than 2 vans. No facilities and no signal. Info sign in the pic basically says “stay at your own risk”. It seems to be fairly level. Good for an overnight but I didn’t stay because it was too early to stop for the day. Documenting since I had not seen it on  the map yet.&#xA;It was curious though that during the 15 min I was there, 3 cars had pulled in turned around and left. I didn’t consider the road being highly trafficked so thought it was weird having so many people use it as a turn around in such a short span of time.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-09 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Natural Source&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/283091 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Wild Camping</type>
  <extensions>
