 <wpt lat="49.880190" lon="-99.557417">
  <ele>374.906005859375</ele>
  <time>2024-07-20 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Camp Huges</name>
  <desc>Named in honor of Sir Sam Hughes, Minister of Militia and Defense (1911-1916), this site houses a parade ground set up for training purposes during the First World War. This terrain is the best preserved in the country and one of the few still in existence in the world. Trenches, firing range, artillery gun positions and observation posts are a reminder of Canada&#39;s determination to prepare soldiers for specific conditions. of the war overseas. Witness to the Canadian military effort, this camp evokes the contribution and sacrifice of those who served during the Great War.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-20 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/284774 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
