 <wpt lat="45.141460" lon="-81.405120">
  <ele></ele>
  <time>2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>305 Dyers Bay Road</name>
  <desc>This is a small section of crown land, the northernmost on the Bruce Peninsula. It hosts a bell cell tower, but a small concealed parking lot can be used to camp for the night. There are no utilities. Service with rogers is mediocre, but with bell is likely very good.&#xA;&#xA;As crown land, you should be able to legally stay here for up to 21 days. After one night&#39;s stay, no issues whatsoever. There are no amenities whatsoever - this is just a parking space&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-18 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: Unknown&#xA;Tent friendly: Unknown&#xA;Pet friendly: Unknown&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/284837 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
