 <wpt lat="59.711246" lon="-133.579110">
  <ele>941.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-21 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>MacDonald Lake Recreation Site</name>
  <desc>Site Description: A small semi-open forested recreation site. 4 units for tenting/RVs/trailers and boat launch.&#xA;&#xA;Driving Directions: Approx. 10km along Rufner Mine Road, north of Atlin.&#xA;Reference: https://www.sitesandtrailsbc.ca/Mobile/Search/search-result.aspx?site=REC3508&amp;districtCode=RDKM&amp;type=Site&#xA;&#xA;We arrived at friday afternoon. All other rec sites around Atlin were full. This site was empty for the whole weekend. We stayed at the place next to the boats ramp. It&#39;s a beautiful place.&#xA;The road behind the bridge is a little rough. 500m before the site beavers flooding the road. We met some locals, who tried to make the road free of water. But it&#39;s possible with a 20ft Campervan, when you are going slow.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-21 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: Pit Toilets&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/284917 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
